{"_id":"2Af5RWZASOzT4cSq","name":"Zombie","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:zombie","level":2,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Cemetery","reputation":7,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead) +3 points","initiative":7,"movementSpeed":"10","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR I p. 417","description":"This is a corpse inhabited by mana and set in motion. It is decomposing but retains its original form. If the eyeballs are dried, they make good quality medicine.\n\nBut not every zombie has its eyes in place. Some individuals are missing parts of their bodies due to decomposition, but as long as their arms and legs are normal, their abilities are not affected.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"3 (10)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":1,"hp":{"value":25,"max":25},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"3 - 4","loot":"Zombie Eye (30G/Red B)"},{"roll":"5+","loot":"Zombie Eye (30G/Red B) x 2"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Zombie","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"2DqgkQKwfKJaQey6","name":"Abyss Corpse","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:abyss-corpse","level":5,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":11,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery Damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"12 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"AB, p. 98","description":"This is an Undead that formed when corpses of creatures left in the Shallow Abyss combined and began to move. Various corpses are chaotically assembled together, forming a horrifying massive body.\n\nA common characteristic is that they form around a core of something that once possessed magical abilities, and sages are searching for the reason why.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arms (Upper Body)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"&#32;","defense":6,"hp":{"value":2,"max":2},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Various (Lower Body)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"&#32;","defense":6,"hp":{"value":3,"max":3},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Upper Body","description":""},{"title":"►Magic (1 system) 5 Level / Magic Power 6 (13)","description":"Abyss Corpse has learned one of the following at level 4: Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic , Divine Magic , Magitech , Fairy Magic , Nature Magic , Summoning Arts , or Abyssal Magic .\nWhen learning Fairy Magic, the types used are &quot;Earth,&quot; &quot;Water/Ice,&quot; &quot;Wind,&quot; and &quot;Darkness.&quot; This remains unchanged even when using the Contract Pattern (see MA, p. 136).\nWhen using Abyssal Magic, enhanced effects are only used for 1 round."},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."},{"title":"Lower Body","description":""},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Size hinders attacks.\nThe Upper Body section gains a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nThis effect is lost if the Lower Body section's HP falls to 0 or below."},{"title":"◯Special Attacks","description":"The Lower Body, composed of combined corpses, performs various attacks. Roll 1d for each melee attack to determine the specific attack method.\n1d Attack Methods 1 – 2 Weapon: A Humanoid arm attacks using a handheld weapon. Use the Accuracy check and damage points as listed in the weapon data. 3 – 4 Glass Bone: Swings a partially melted large arm with visible bones violently. Accuracy check remains unchanged, and if the attack hits, damage is increased by +5 points, but simultaneously the large arm breaks off, dealing 5 points of fixed damage to Lower Body section itself. Nothing happens if the attack misses. 5 – 6 Cursed Fangs: Bites with cursed fangs. Accuracy check is reduced by -1, and damage is reduced by 1 point. However, when the attack hits, the damage dealt becomes curse magic damage."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Tainted Bones (50G/Red B)"},{"roll":"7 - 9","loot":"Chipped Fangs (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Artifacts of the Dead (500G/White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Abyss Corpse","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"30ZcV7C28OXxYGQI","name":"Skeleton Heavy Archer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:skeleton-heavy-archer","level":6,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":8,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"VC","description":"It is a Skeleton Archer with a body length of about 2 meters. The bow used is also large, increasing the threat level.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bow","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":48,"max":48},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Bone Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"► Bow","description":"With &quot;Range: 2 (30m),&quot; it makes a Shooting Attack with a bow. Its Accuracy check and damage are the same as a normal attack."},{"title":"◯ Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"It can shoot with Bow into a skirmish without causing stray shots, and shoot through skirmishes to attack opponents on the far side."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Sturdy Bones (30G/Red B) x 1d"},{"roll":"7+","loot":"Magical Bones (250/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Skeleton Heavy Archer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"3X8vJXO6baO56EWU","name":"Warring Ash","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:warring-ash","level":7,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Wilderness","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"-/20 (Floating)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR III p. 364","description":"The ashes of a corpse burnt to ashes, leaving behind a grudge and becoming Undead. It rarely occurs when a person burned to death in a fire is left unattended or when a corpse is burned carelessly in the open. It is rare for a corpse that has been officially cremated to become Undead. These ashes rise and move in whirling zephyrs. They are full of resentment and attack the living without regard.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":53,"max":53},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity, ◯ Wind Immunity, ◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Ash Body","description":"Blunt weapons treat the Defense of Warring Ash as 5 points higher.\nThrows deal no damage and have no effect.\nAny damage that is not of the recovery effect type cannot be critical."},{"title":"◯ Shadow Sneak","description":"It is not subject to any movement blocking (see CR II, p. 59) and is not restricted in any way when attempting to leave the skirmish."},{"title":"► Cover with Ash/9 (16)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Within &quot;Range: Touch,&quot; it covers &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; with its own body and suffocates it. The target suffers 2d+7 poison magic damage. In addition, the target will not be able to make any vocalizations for 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"► Gale of Ashes/9 (16)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Warring Ash rushes through the air in a whirlwind, tearing through anything it touches. Within &quot;Range/Area: 1 (20m) / Breakthrough &quot;, the targets are dealt 2d+5 Wind magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Corrupted Ash (300G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Warring Ash","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"42oNpIQ418PGz86f","name":"Abyss Marchers","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:abyss-marchers","level":14,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade common","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":17,"weakness":23,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery Damage +3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"12 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"18 (25)","willpower":"18 (25)","source":"AB, p. 101","description":"Abyss Marchers are a funeral procession mourning the dead who were swallowed by the Shallow Abyss and became contaminated by the Abyss, turning them into the dead themselves.\n\nThey constantly lament both the original dead and themselves, finding solace in gloomy hymns. They continue their endless march, harboring resentment towards everything they encounter, especially envying the living.\n\nWhile they are typically only encountered within a Shallow, if they were to emerge outside, it would surely cause great chaos.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arm","accuracy":"17 (24)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"&#32;","defense":14,"hp":{"value":4,"max":4},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Swarm Advance","description":"This monster is not affected by movement blocking and can leave the skirmish area without requiring a withdraw action.\nIt cannot be targeted by Throw or similar effects.\nCannot be affected by effects other than damage that target &quot;1 Character.&quot; It cannot be affected by &quot;target: 1 Character X&quot; effects.\nWhen targeted by &quot;target: 1 Entire Character&quot; effects, it can automatically gain immunity by spending 1d HP points. This can be decided after resistance checks are performed.\nWhen targeted by weapon attacks or effects that deal damage with &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, it can automatically nullify them by spending &quot;1d&quot; HP points. This can be decided after calculating the applied damage.\nWhen affected by wide-area effects with maximum target numbers or becoming the target of damage, it automatically becomes the target while all other characters in the area are removed from targeting. Combat Feat [ Magic Control ] and similar effects are nullified. If multiple characters with the [◯Swarm Advance] ability exist in the area, only one character is randomly selected to receive the effect.\nWhen affected with &quot;Area: Line &quot; effects, applied damage is halved (rounded up) (quarter damage if succeeded on &quot;Resistance: Half&quot;). However, even if not selected as a target, it automatically gets caught in the effect."},{"title":"◯Gloomy Chant / 17 (24) / Willpower / Half","description":"This effect triggers automatically once at the start of this monster's turn. Within &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; it sings a cursed hymn to &quot;Range: All Areas (50m radius) / All&quot;, dealing magical damage to HP and MP. The damage is 2d+4 points inside the Shallow Abyss and 2d points outside of the Shallow.\nAdditionally, targets who fail their resistance check suffer a -1 penalty to all skill checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round), that is until this monster's turn comes again.\nThis effect and damage are of the psychic type. Furthermore, characters classified as &quot; Undead &quot; are immune to this effect and damage."},{"title":"►Simultaneous Attack","description":"Makes a melee attack against any number of characters in the same skirmish."},{"title":"►Breakthrough / 16 (23) / Evasion / Negates","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 1(12m) / Breakthrough &quot;, deals 2d+16 points of physical damage to the target and knocks them prone (note that this effect can be used even in a melee due to the [◯Swarm Advance] ability)."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Artifacts of the Dead (500G/White A)"},{"roll":"9 - 11","loot":"Valuable Heirloom (1,000G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Gorgeous Heirloom (6,000G/Gold White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Abyss Marchers","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"46raO3CpM4Wu9hvX","name":"Vampire Hound","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:vampire-hound","level":5,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"18 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"GR, Battle Mastery p. 128","description":"A ferocious Undead dog under the influence of a Vampire. Drinking the fresh blood of others causes them to attack with greater frenzy.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":42,"max":42},"mp":{"value":15,"max":15}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Vampiric Madness / 7 (14) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"When attacking, the Vampire Hound drains blood from its target, the smell of which causes it to become frenzied.\nIf an attack hits, the target makes a Fortitude Check immediately after damage is dealt. If it fails, the Vampire Hound gains a +1 to its Accuracy and damage, as well as a -1 penalty to its Evasion, for 3 minutes (18 rounds).\nThis effect is cumulative and can stack up to four times."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Beast Skeleton (60G / Red B)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Corrupted Ash (300G / Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Vampire Hound","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"5TIsecQTD4AeqOof","name":"Dry Corpse","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dry-corpse","level":3,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Cemetery","reputation":8,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR I p. 418","description":"Like Zombies , this is a corpse in motion, but it differs from Zombie in that its body tissues are dry and tight, giving it the appearance of a skeletal Human from a distance.\n\nThey are light and agile. If you approach them carelessly, they will cut you down to pieces in no time, and you may lose your life.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+2","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":2,"hp":{"value":25,"max":25},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If a Dry Corpse successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack against the same target."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Tainted Bones (50G/Red B)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Tainted Skull (300G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dry Corpse","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"7QrQCoWghmptru8p","name":"Mice Ball","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:mice-ball","level":9,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Sewers, Labyrinths","reputation":15,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (when deals damage) +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"20 (Rotation)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 130","description":"The &quot;Soulscarred Core&quot; is a horrific power accidentally created during research into Spiritualism Magic for generating Undead. It drains the life from small creatures around it and animates their corpses, gathering them around itself.\n\nWhen it was carelessly abandoned, it found its way into the city's sewers, where it began attracting mice, killing them, and using their corpses to form a spherical mass known as a Mice Ball.\n\nOnce it reaches a certain size, the &quot;Soulscarred Core&quot; splits into two smaller Mice Balls, which then continue the process of attracting and killing rats to grow larger. As a result, it's estimated that a considerable number of these are now writhing in the sewers. There are also reports of them escaping and spreading damage to other areas. Those who escape to forests are believed to be creating different types of Balls by gathering and killing small forest animals.\n\nWhile the leak of the &quot;Soulscarred Core&quot; has been kept secret from the general public, it remains a well-known scandal of the Haroon Magical Research Kingdom Academy. The academy is eager to recover these cores and offers rewards for both intact Core and destroyed Core fragments.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":79,"max":79},"mp":{"value":31,"max":31}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity, Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 9 points","description":"At the end of its turn, HP recovers by 9 points. If HP falls to 0 or below, this ability is lost."},{"title":"►Crushing Fangs / 12 (19) / Evasion / Negates","description":"The mice that make up the body explode, dealing 2d+15 points of Curse physical damage in &quot;Range: Caster&quot; to &quot;Target: 1 area (5m radius) / 15.&quot;\nWhen using this effect, the Mice Ball's Defense is reduced by 3 points for the next 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"When this monster's HP is reduced below 0, for each point below zero, the Loot Determination 2d roll result is reduced by 1."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"6 - 8","loot":"Fragment of Soulscarred Core (300G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"9 - 11","loot":"Fragment of Soulscarred Core (300G/Gold A) x 1d"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Soulscarred Core (3,000G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Mice Ball","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"7RzwDgLDnaCbtdy6","name":"Blood Sucker","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:blood-sucker","level":6,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Regional Dialect","habitat":"Various","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR II p. 372","description":"A person drained by a Lesser Vampire Nosferatu then revived into a subservient unlife, a Blood Sucker is still a dangerous monster to encounter.\n\nWith pale skin and bloody eyes, they lack the grace of their sires and stand out as something unnatural. Their memories are distorted. They will attack humans and animals alike to stave off hunger and thirst.\n\nDue to their vulnerability to sunlight, Blood Suckers move and attack solely at night.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":49,"max":49},"mp":{"value":6,"max":6}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If a Blood Sucker successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack against the same target."},{"title":"⏩ Gaze/7 (14)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Blood Suckers may attempt to paralyze with &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; within &quot;Range/Area: 50m / Target &quot;. If the target fails to resist the Gaze, they are paralyzed for 10 seconds (1 round) and cannot take any Minor Actions or active combat feats.\nThis unique skill can be used only once per round."},{"title":"► Vampire Bite/7 (14)/Evasion/Negates","description":"The Blood Sucker bites a target in the same skirmish, dealing 2d+4 Physical damage. The Blood Sucker heals HP equal to the applied damage dealt."},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 3 points","description":"At the end of each round, a Blood Sucker recovers 3 HP. This has no effect if the Blood Sucker is at 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Vampire Body","description":"As long as a Blood Sucker is under sunlight, it takes 6 magic damage at the end of its turn and receives a -2 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion Checks. This damage cannot be reduced in any way, and the Blood Sucker cannot use their [ ◯ Regeneration] unique skill."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Corrupted Ash (300G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Blood Sucker","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"8L0jxUFpvcQNyRw7","name":"Undead General","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:undead-general","level":14,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":16,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"23","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"17 (24)","source":"CR III p. 370","description":"The Undead Generals were specially created by ancient wizard-kings to guard their treasures.\n\nThese warriors are skilled at launching swift and powerful attacks, making them formidable in melee combat. However, they possess low intelligence and can only carry out orders. Still guarding the wizard-king's secret underground laboratories and treasure vaults, they are an extremely formidable adversary for any adventurers.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"18 (25)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"18 (25)","defense":18,"hp":{"value":128,"max":128},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Resistance","description":"The Undead General gains a +4 bonus when it makes a Willpower roll against any psychic type spell or unique skill."},{"title":"◯ Bone Body","description":"An Undead General is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"► 4 Attacks (At Random)","description":"The Undead General makes four attacks, swinging the weapon around in both hands. For each attack, the target is chosen at random from the list of possible melee attackers."},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack II","description":"If an Undead General successfully hits a target in melee, they may make a second attack. They can make a third attack against the same target if a second attack hits."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +12 points."},{"title":"🗨 △ Cover I","description":"The effect is the same as the combat feat [ Cover I ]."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Well-kept Weapon (1,000G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"2 - 12","loot":"Well-kept Weapon (1,000G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Royal Treasured Sword (8,000G/Gold Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Undead General","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"AFgi81ha9CX37a9m","name":"Mummy","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:mummy","level":9,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"CR II p. 375","description":"Guardians of the wizard-kings of ancient times, Mummies are dried corpses wholly covered with bandages. Their loyalty is unwavering even in death, and they will mercilessly attack anyone venturing into their king's crypt. A Mummy can also cause a debilitating curse just from touching the living, so contact is highly discouraged.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arm","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":77,"max":77},"mp":{"value":30,"max":30}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two Arm attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯ Decaying Curse","description":"If an Arm attack hits, it will reduce the target's maximum HP by the same amount as the applied damage (never less than 0). If a character's maximum HP is reduced to 0 in this way, they immediately die (no Death Check needed).\nThis effect is treated as a Curse type and is permanent. This effect can also be removed with a spell such as the [ Remove Curse ] spell (which requires a success value of at least 20), but it is also automatically removed if the Mummy who bestowed the curse is defeated. A character who dies with a maximum HP of 0 can only be revived after the curse has been removed."},{"title":"◯ Fire Vulnerability","description":"When the Mummy is hit by Fire-type damage, it takes an extra 3 damage."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Yellowed Golden Ring (1,000G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Yellowed Golden Bracelet (2,000G/Gold White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Mummy","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"B8NIbmGn6shF1ISY","name":"Rottenfolk","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rottenfolk","level":7,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Natural History of Dilfrum (2.0 supplement), p. 166","description":"After the Diabolic Triumph, a group of Barbarous mistakenly used a Runefolk generator they had taken from Humanoids. By inserting the corpses of Humanoids and Barbarous, they created corpse puppets. Although they have a Humanoid shape, a Rottenfolk is a grotesque entity with various Barbarous parts mixed in, making it far from human. It possesses enough intelligence to understand and act on commands, making it valuable as it can be ordered and controlled even by those who are not magicians.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":63,"max":63},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Lifeforge Magitech 7 Level/Magic Power 8 (15)","description":"Rottenfolk can cast Magitech spells. However, instead of consuming MP, their maximum HP and current HP will decrease by the amount consumed. If their maximum HP reaches 0, the Rottenfolk will cease to work and become immobile."},{"title":"► Gunfire / 10 (17) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Makes a Ranged Attack with a gun. Range is 2(40m) and Max Magazine is 3."},{"title":"◯ Hawk Eye &amp; Precise Shot","description":"Attacks fired into a skirmish cannot cause stray shots. Also, a Rottenfolk can shoot through cover."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Magisphere (Small) (100G/-) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 11","loot":"Dirty Weapon (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Well-Kept Weapon (1,000G/Gold Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rottenfolk","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"BnkqQJUtyFRyckKu","name":"Bone Knight","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bone-knight","level":9,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Wilderness, Cemetery","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"30 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 374","description":"At first glance, this appears to be a mounted knight in armor. However, as the Bone Knight draws near, it's easy to see the skull peering out of the armor, its malice towards the living almost tangible. An old knight from the Magic Civilization age is searching for their lost lord and will let nothing get in their way. Though dead for a while, a Bone Knight's swordsmanship and magical prowess remain as sharp as they were, making the undead knight a truly fearsome foe.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon (Rider)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":77,"max":77},"mp":{"value":58,"max":58}},{"style":"Hoof (Horse)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":63,"max":63},"mp":{"value":28,"max":28}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity , ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Rider","description":""},{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 8 Level /Magic Power 11 (18)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], and [ Universal Metamagic ]."},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two Weapon attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"Horse","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +2 • None","description":"The enormity of the Horse prevents foes from attacking the Knight.\nThe Rider receives a +2 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. When the Horse falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Ghostly Reins (900G/White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Bone Knight Helmet (4,200G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bone Knight","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"CJCW6Dr6DzqSoKKU","name":"Adapsia","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:adapsia","level":5,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Regional Dialect","habitat":"Forests, Mountain, Wilderness","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR III p. 363","description":"This is an undead person with a corpse-like body. They maintain the same appearance as before they were born and are almost indistinguishable from the living.\n\nFor some reason, their souls were not reincarnated but remained in the corpse. Some resent the world and try to bring misfortune upon it, while others maintain their reason and intelligence and leave their homes to exist alone in remote places. It is said they gather together in some places to form pseudo-families.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":39,"max":39},"mp":{"value":16,"max":16}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity , ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Fire Vulnerability","description":"When the Adapsia is hit by Fire-type damage, it takes an extra 3 damage."},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Broken Memento (500G/White A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Memento (1,000G/White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Adapsia","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"CWC9IiPs9ktvyI5g","name":"Dragon Corpse","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dragon-corpse","level":9,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs) / 15 (Flying)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Ancient Blue (SW2.5 supplement) p. 137","description":"This is an Undead creature with soulscars inhabiting a dragon's corpse. It constantly emits miasma from its mouth and wings. While its entire body continues to decay and will eventually cease moving as a corpse given enough time, there have been reported sightings of it continuing to move like other Undead, depending on environmental conditions and other external factors.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Body)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":82,"max":82},"mp":{"value":16,"max":16}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":66,"max":66},"mp":{"value":10,"max":10}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":66,"max":66},"mp":{"value":10,"max":10}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"►Miasma Breath / 11 (18) / Fortitude / Half","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot &quot;, exhale a toxic mass at &quot;Target: 1 area (3m radius)/5&quot;, dealing 2d+8 points of Poison magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"Wings","description":""},{"title":"🗨All-Out Attack","description":"Increase damage by +8 points. Simultaneously, receive a -3 penalty to your Evasion check."},{"title":"►Decaying Healing Energy / 10 (17) / Fortitude / Temporary","description":"Fill the surroundings with energy, afflicting nearby enemies with poison. With &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 area (3m radius / 10)&quot;, targets receive a -1 penalty to Poison and Disease resistance checks for 3 minutes (18 rounds). This effect stacks up to -4 (even if successful on resistance checks because of Temporary resistance)."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9 - 11","loot":"Miasmic Rotten Flesh (600G/Red A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Miasma Covered Rotten Flesh (2,000G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dragon Corpse","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"D5CLoQ5iIKSWcVQm","name":"Dedarium","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dedarium","level":6,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":13,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Silver weapon damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"13","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 125","description":"This Undead creature is a fusion of mana and the grudges of the dead. Its insubstantial ghost body is covered with small insect carcasses, giving it a humanoid form.\n\nWhile a normal weapon may only peel off a part of the insect carcasses, it will not affect the ghost body. Only silver or magic weapons can inflict damage on it (see CR III, p. 327).\n\nThese creatures act out of resentment towards the living. When they encounter their targets, they mercilessly attack, showering them with the echoes of their curses. Sometimes, multiple creatures will appear and surround their target, creating a terrifying chorus of sounds.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":45,"max":45},"mp":{"value":12,"max":12}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"►Resenting Sounds / 8 (15) / Willpower / Half","description":"When using this effect, the monster consumes 10 points of its own HP. It shakes its entire body, rubbing the carcasses of the insects that form it against each other, and resenting sounds come out.\nWithin &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; it deals 2d+6 Curse magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 Area (5m Radius) / 15.&quot; This ability does not affect Undead characters.\nIf other Dedariums are in the effect area, they cannot perform [►Resenting Sounds] for the following 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"⏩Vindictive Resonance / 8 (15) / Willpower / Negates","description":"This effect can be used only once in the following 10 seconds (1 round) in the turn that comes within the effect range of [►Resenting Sounds] performed by another Dedarium.\nThe whole body trembles finely in tune with the [►Resenting Sounds] used and resonates with the sound of the curse.\nThis effect will cause 2 Curse magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (5m Radius) / 15&quot; within &quot;Range: Caster.&quot; This ability does not affect Undead characters."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Crystal Tears of Resentment (500G/White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dedarium","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"EtVYabsJorF1kRGW","name":"Skull Bird","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:skull-bird","level":3,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Abandoned Houses","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"10/16 (Flying)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR II p. 369","description":"This is an undead monster raptor. It has no flesh left but only bones.\n\nThey are often found in ruins in swarms, or they can be accompanied by stronger undead.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Beak","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":19,"max":19},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Bone Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"🗨 Piercing Attack","description":"When a melee attack deals physical damage to a target, the target's Defense is halved (rounded up) for that attack. At risk, the monster takes a -1 penalty to Evasion checks."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Soulscarred Bird Bones (50G/Red B)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Soulscarred Bird Skull (250G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Skull Bird","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FGwmJ9Bn4gygQDSQ","name":"Lantern Bird","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lantern-bird","level":5,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Plains","reputation":12,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"-/15 (Flying)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 124","description":"This Undead creature is often spotted in forests and plains during the night, with numerous sightings reported on the Farveld Plains of the Burlight Region. It resembles a medium-sized bird, comprised solely of bones, and its head emits an eerie blue phosphorescent glow.\n\nAn enchanted curse resides within its glowing head, and once the skull's magical power is depleted, it can be utilized as a material for crafting a Protective Lantern (see Natural History of Burlight p. 42).","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":35,"max":35},"mp":{"value":16,"max":16}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight","description":"A Lantern Bird receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"⏩Fear Curse / 8 (15) / Willpower / Half","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 1(10m)/Target,&quot; the Lantern Bird whispers a word of fear curse into &quot;Target: 1 Character's&quot; ear and inflicts 1d magical damage to the target's MP.\nUsing this ability consumes 3 points of MP. Also, once the target makes a successful Willpower check, this ability cannot be used again on this turn."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If the character has 3 or more MP left when they defeat the Lantern Bird, the loot item &quot;Bird Skull Without Power&quot; is changed to &quot;Soulscarred Bird Skull (250G/Red A).&quot;"},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Soulscarred Bird Bones (50G/red B)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Bird Skull Without Power (500G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lantern Bird","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FypyYfomCHiRqQto","name":"Banshee","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:banshee","level":9,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":12,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Energy damage +3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"-/21(Floating)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR III p. 366","description":"A Banshee is the vengeful spirit of a woman who died in sorrow after suffering a terrible betrayal, seeking to share her fate with others. Its screams can shake even the most stoic of adventurers, and it is said that death comes to those who've heard the wail of a Banshee. Though they tend to appear as a beautiful woman, Banshees turn as ugly as a mummy when unleashing their wail on others. Upon defeat, a Banshee will disappear entirely, leaving behind only beautiful crystals, physical remnants of their powerful emotions.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":72,"max":72},"mp":{"value":73,"max":73}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"Banshee can perform two Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 7 Level/Magic Power 10 (27)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"A Banshee can use the Combat Feat [ Universal Metamagic ]."},{"title":"► Maddening Scream/13 (20)/Willpower/ Negates","description":"The Banshee makes a high-pitched wail within &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; causing everyone within a &quot;Target: All Areas (20m Radius)/All&quot; to go mad. A character affected by this effect must randomly select a target for their attacks, casting spells, and other effects. The character is free to choose actions, use Minor Actions, declare active combat feats, etc.\nThe target of an action taken by a frenzied character is chosen at random after checking possible targets by the range and other conditions just before the Skill Check for the action is taken. This effect lasts for 3 minutes (18 rounds), but it also disappears when the affected character inflicts a total of 45 points of applied damage to a character in their own faction. A character released from the effect of applied damage accumulation cannot receive the effect of [ ► Maddening Scream] for 1 day afterward (if the effect is released by any other method, it may receive the effect anew). If a character who has been affected by this effect is affected again, the duration of the effect is refreshed, but the accumulated applied damage is until the effect is removed as it is.\nThis effect is treated as Psychic type.\nBanshee can use this ability only once per round."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Crystal Tears of Resentment (500G/White A)"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Crystal Tears of Sorrow (1,000G/White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Banshee","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FzOhNO5j7gyoDN6D","name":"Night Ghoul","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:night-ghoul","level":10,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":14,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Silver Weapon Damage +3","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"-/24 (Flight)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"BM","description":"This foul monster is a Ghoul that can fly at night with bat-like wings on its back. The wings are thought to be evidence of a Soulscar mutation from feeding on corpses.\n\nFlying in the darkness of the night, they find their poor victims and snatch them away.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":88,"max":88},"mp":{"value":25,"max":25}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Paralyzing Poison / 12 (19) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If a Claw attack hits and deals at least 1 applied damage, the target has a -2 penalty to Evasion checks for 30 seconds (3 rounds). This effect is not cumulative.\nThis effect is of a Poison type."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Night Ghoul receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Ghoul Toxin Extract (20G / Gold Red B) x 2"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Ghoul Coin (500G / Gold A)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Rare Ghoul Coin (350G / Gold A) x 1d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Night Ghoul","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"G7hbHorR4xJL9LPQ","name":"Redish Dedarium","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:redish-dedarium","level":7,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":14,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Silver weapon damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"13","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 125","description":"This Dedarium variant is known for its notable strength and intense hostility. The surface of these insects is adorned with vibrant colors, including shades of red and yellow, and they emit a faint glow. Additionally, they possess a larger body size compared to their counterparts.\n\nThese creatures often appear alongside the regular Dedarium and are considered a plague that resonates with a sense of vengeance. In fact, there have been instances where entire villages have been decimated by their presence.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":60,"max":60},"mp":{"value":25,"max":25}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"►Resenting Sounds / 8 (15) / Willpower / Half","description":"When using this effect, the monster consumes 10 points of its own HP. It shakes its entire body, rubbing the carcasses of the insects that form it against each other, and resenting sounds come out.\nWithin &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; it deals 2d+7 Curse magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 Area (5m Radius) / 15.&quot; This ability does not affect Undead characters.\nIf other Dedariums are in the effect area, they cannot perform [►Resenting Sounds] for the following 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"⏩Vindictive Resonance / 8 (15) / Willpower / Negates","description":"This effect can be used only once in the following 10 seconds (1 round) in the turn that comes within the effect range of [►Resenting Sounds] performed by another Dedarium.\nThe whole body trembles finely in tune with the [►Resenting Sounds] used and resonates with the sound of the curse.\nThis effect will cause 3 Curse magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (5m Radius) / 15&quot; within &quot;Range: Caster.&quot; This ability does not affect Undead characters."},{"title":"◯Strong Resentment","description":"The damage of [⏩Vindictive Resonance] by any Dedarium made in response to [►Resenting Sounds] used by this monster will be 3 points."},{"title":"►Collect Dead Bodies","description":"The Redish Dedarium sucks the immortal life force from the surrounding Dedariums and makes them its own. Within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; against &quot;Target: 1 Area (5m Radius)/Space,&quot; it can assign up to 20 points of damage to the target's Dedariums as fixed damage (it cannot deal more damage than their current HP), and heal its own HP by the total number of damage dealt."},{"title":"►Great Resenting Sounds / 10 (17) / Willpower / Half","description":"This ability can only be used when there are no other Dedariums on the battlefield, and it is always used when that condition is reached. The whole body of Redish Dedarium shakes violently, rubbing the carcasses of the insects that form itself hard against each other, making the sound of a curse that resents the living.\nWithin &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; this ability deals 2d+12 Curse magic damage to &quot;Target: All Areas (30m Radius) / All.&quot; This effect does not affect Undead characters. After using this effect, the Redish Dedarium takes 20 fixed damage to its HP."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Crystal Tears of Resentment (500G/White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Crystal Tears of Resentment (500G/White A) x 2"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Redish Dedarium","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"H2oaPrSc88L92Prp","name":"Skeleton Soldier","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:skeleton-soldier","level":5,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":7,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"21","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR II p. 370","description":"It is a Skeleton armed with a large weapon and armor. It aggressively attacks and tries to eliminate any approaching creature.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":36,"max":36},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Bone Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Sturdy Bones (30G/Red B)"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Magical Bones (250G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Skeleton Soldier","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HLiUqIk97t13v1tq","name":"Weavewraith Warrior","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:weavewraith-warrior","level":12,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common","habitat":"Cold Regions, Shallows","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"-/15 (Floating)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"AB, p. 100","description":"The Korgana region, where the Abyss gapes open, lies at the northernmost point of the Alframe continent. Being exposed to the cold currents of the Abyss Sea, it is an extremely cold place.\n\nIt is said that these Undead are what remains of warriors who, fighting against the Abyss in such cold, were ultimately consumed by the Shallow Abyss when their strength failed them.\n\nTheir transparent bodies are cold enough to freeze anything they touch, and they wear winter attire consisting of fur-lined coats and trousers, hats, gloves, boots, and scarves. These garments too have become completely frozen, and rather than providing warmth, they inflict a crushing coldness that freezes anything they come into contact with.\n\nHaving projected only their fighting spirit into the Shallow, they have become distorted. They harbor hatred for living beings, especially those with warm blood flowing through them, and attempt to drag them into the realm of the dead.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"&#32;","defense":16,"hp":{"value":8,"max":8},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited 2 Actions","description":"It can perform two Major Actions per round, but they are limited to one melee attack with a weapon and one [►3 Attires]."},{"title":"►3 Attires","description":"Three randomly selected attires perform attacks. Which ones attack is determined randomly by rolling 1d and consulting the table, but the same garment cannot be selected multiple times. Such rolls should be redone to ensure three different garments are selected.\nAll attacks are performed with &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Target &quot; against &quot;Target: 1 Character.&quot; The GM determines the target for each acting garment (they can be the same or different). Targets can use resistance or evasion abilities at the specified values for resistance or dodging. Effects and damage are &quot;Water/Ice or Curse type&quot; inside the Shallow Abyss and &quot;Water/Ice type&quot; outside the Shallow.\nThe ability score reduction effect lasts for 3 minutes (18 rounds) and stacks. If an ability score reaches 0 through this effect, the target dies. For monster data characters, the GM should reduce the Success Value by -1 for actions they determine are related to that ability score. The monster dies if it receives three reduction effects to the same ability score.\n1d | Attack | Details |\n1 | Hat Squeezes Head / 14 (21) / Willpower / Negates | Reduces the target's Intelligence by 6 points. |\n2 | Gloves Squeeze Hands / 14 (21) / Willpower / Negates | Reduces the target's Dexterity by 6 points. |\n3 | Boots Squeeze Feet / 14(21) / Willpower / Negates | Reduces the target's Agility by 6 points. |\n4 | Scarf Choking Neck / 14(21) / Willpower / Negates | Deals 2d+12 points of magic damage to the target. |\n5 | Jacket Hits Body / 15 (22) / Evasion / Negates | Deals 2d+16 points of physical damage to the target. |\n6 | Pants Hit Body / 15 (22) / Evasion / Negates | Deals 2d+16 points of physical damage to the target. |"}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Crystal Tears of Regret (250G/White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Winter Attires (720G/White A)"},{"roll":"9 - 11","loot":"Thick Winter Attire (2,160G/White S)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Fine Winter Attire (6,480G/White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Weavewraith Warrior","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Id7uYM9Br0sIJyxU","name":"Bloodling","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bloodling","level":3,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Regional Dialect","habitat":"Various","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"12/24(Flying)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR III p. 362","description":"Bloodlings are a species of Blood Suckers created by Nosferatu , but it is clearly an inferior species. When Bloodlings are born, only a certain percentage of them survive, and the reason for this is unclear.\n\nBloodlings take on the form of a human with bat wings for arms. At night, they fly around, emitting a high-pitched, sad cry, targeting the weakest enemies.\n\nNosferatu can be expected to be nearby wherever these creatures are found.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+2","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":24,"max":24},"mp":{"value":6,"max":6}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Vampire Bite/4 (11)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Bites an enemy character in the skirmish in which it resides, dealing 2d-1 physical damage. The Bloodling heals HP equal to the applied damage dealt."},{"title":"◯ Vampire Body","description":"As long as a Bloodling is under sunlight, it takes 3 magic damage at the end of its turn and receives a -2 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion Checks. This damage cannot be reduced in any way."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Bloodling receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Corrupted Ash (300G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bloodling","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Ju6RsvtKPtWttNEb","name":"Ghost Train","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghost-train","level":7,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"30 (Flying)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 127","description":"This is the ghost train that has become the talk of the Dorden Region. The patterns of when and where it appears are a complete mystery, and its purpose has not been revealed.\n\nIt is said to appear out of nowhere on foggy nights, on the rails or at deserted stations, accompanied by a whistle. It stops in front of living beings and opens its passenger car doors as if inviting them in.\n\nThe passenger cars are occupied by insubstantial, translucent passengers. While it doesn't refuse those who want to board, if someone with hostile intentions approaches, it opens its windows and throws Stones, attacking them.\n\nIt's completely unknown where those who board are taken, but rumors say no one has ever returned alive.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None (Engine Room)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":69,"max":69},"mp":{"value":54,"max":54}},{"style":"Stone (Cabin x 3)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":86,"max":86},"mp":{"value":22,"max":22}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity, ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"◯Ghost Train Body","description":"When receiving damage from blunt weapons, it is treated as if its Defense is 5 points higher. When receiving magic damage, the total damage is first automatically halved (if it resists a &quot;Resistance: Half&quot; spell, it becomes one-quarter)."},{"title":"Engine Room","description":""},{"title":"►Whistle of Grudge / 9 (16) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Blows a whistle that curses living beings. Targets in &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;All Area (30m radius)/All&quot; will have their Vitality score reduced by -1 point for 6 hours (this also reduces maximum HP and Fortitude). This effect is cumulative, and if Vitality falls to 0 or below due to this effect, the target immediately gains 5 soulscars and dies.\nThis effect is Curse type. Using this ability consumes 6 MP from the Engine Room section."},{"title":"►Steam Blast / 9 (16) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Blasts a strange steam with a cold and eerie sensation. At &quot;Range: 1 (10m)&quot; targets in &quot;1 area (3m radius)/5&quot; take 2d+8 points of Water/Ice magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"Cabin","description":""},{"title":"►Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"A Cabin can make two Stone attacks each round, though each attack requires its Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯Throwing Attack","description":"The Stone attack is treated as a Thrown Attack with a range of 1 (10m)."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Broken Memento (500G/White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Memento (1,000G/White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghost Train","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KAhk2ZIwdNxfMk2L","name":"Revenant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:revenant","level":0,"monsterType":"","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":8,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead) +3 points","initiative":-2,"movementSpeed":"※","fortitude":"※","willpower":"※","source":"CR I p. 416","description":"A Revenant is an undead being created by the death of an impure soul. Constant resurrections scar one's soul and certain spirits can rise on their own with enough soulscars. Humanoids, Barbarous, animals, and mythical beasts can be Revenants.\n\nA Revenant has an intense hatred of the living and will kill without discrimination. If a Revenant is reduced to 0 HP or lower, it is utterly destroyed and cannot be revived.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon, etc.","accuracy":"※ +2","damage":"※ +2","evasion":"※ -2","defense":0,"hp":{"value":0,"max":0},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Past Life","description":"This monster's strength depends on its strength before it is reborn as a Revenant. In the various numerical fields, apply the numerical value of the monster before it was reborn to the places marked with &quot; ※ &quot;.\nThe level of this monster is equal to &quot;Previous Level + 1&quot;. Revenant also inherits combat feats and unique skills. However, it cannot cast spells."},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 3 points","description":"At the end of each round, a Revenant recovers 3 HP. This has no effect if the Revenant is at 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 10","loot":"Tainted Bones (50G/Red B)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Tainted Skull (300G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Revenant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"LearNcKMJm3IoFaB","name":"Veil of Darkness","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:veil-of-darkness","level":10,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":16,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"-/20(Flying)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"AB, p. 100","description":"This is a collective of vengeful spirits that mainly appears in the Shallow Abysses. Layers of dark grudges create darkness.\n\nIf adventurers witness phenomena such as &quot;sudden darkness while walking in the Shallow&quot; or &quot;a partially darkened sky in the distance,&quot; this monster is strongly suspected to be the cause.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"&#32;","defense":12,"hp":{"value":9,"max":9},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight II","description":"A Veil of Darkness receives a +2 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯Veil of Darkness/Can't","description":"With &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: All areas (30m radius) / Space&quot;, covers the area in darkness and blocks vision. Characters without Darkvision ability in their &quot;Perception: Five Senses&quot; cannot see their surroundings without lighting.\nAdditionally, characters within this effect's range must roll 1d at the start of their turn and suffer effects from the table below. Effects last for 10 seconds (1 round) until the start of their next turn. However, characters who meet any of the following conditions are immune to these effects: &quot;has 'Shallow' in Habitat&quot;, &quot;Classification: Daemon &quot;, or &quot;race is Abyssborn .&quot;\n1d | Effect |\n1 | The character becomes blind regardless of lighting conditions pr their perception abilities. |\n2 | If the character lacks Darkvision ability in their &quot;Perception: Five Senses&quot;, they become\nblind even with lighting present. |\n3-4 | The character's perception abilities are significantly reduced regardless of lighting conditions or\ntheir perception abilities. They receive a -2 penalty to all action checks. |\n5-6 | No particular negative effects. |\nEven if multiple of these monsters exist simultaneously, effect determination occurs only once per character's turn."},{"title":"►Impact from the Void / 12 (19) / Willpower / Half","description":"Within &quot;Range: Touch&quot; deals &quot;2d+12&quot; points of Bludgeoning magic damage to a &quot;Target: 1 Character.&quot;\nIf the target fails their resistance against this effect, they must immediately roll 1d to redetermine the effects of [◯Veil of Darkness]. The newly determined effects persist until the target's next turn.\nThe target may choose not to resist this effect."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Crystal Tears of Regret (250G/White A)"},{"roll":"9 - 12","loot":"Crystal Tears of Resentment (500G/White A)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Crystal of Malice (8,000G/White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Veil of Darkness","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"N9eMNohvEr1VvQI5","name":"Iron Maiden","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:iron-maiden","level":12,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Labyrinths, Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"-/15 (Floating)","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"15 (22)","source":"BM","description":"The Iron Maiden is a torture device in the shape of a woman's body, affected by mana and granted sentience. Its entire body is made of iron and is hollow inside. The hollowed-out body is covered with countless thorns, which lock up people and squeeze out their blood, causing them to suffer and bleed.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"16 (23)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":15,"hp":{"value":113,"max":113},"mp":{"value":36,"max":36}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Iron Body","description":"The Iron Maiden is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"► Lock Up / 15 (22) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Traps a &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; at &quot;Range: Touch&quot; inside its own body.\nThe Iron Maiden cannot attempt to [ ► Lock Up] a new target while one is trapped inside. The Iron Maiden may release the imprisoned character with a Minor Action. Unless it declares [ 🗨 Hold On], the trapped character automatically escapes on its turn."},{"title":"🗨 Hold On","description":"Closes its own lid for 10 seconds (1 round). By doing so, the Iron Maiden gains +5 points to its Defense.\nIf this declaration is made first, [ ► Lock Up] cannot be used later. It is possible to use [ ► Lock Up] first and declare this ability immediately after the first use of [ 🗨 Hold On].\nWhen this declaration is made, [ 🗨 Hold On] deals 2d+14 points of physical damage to the trapped character, if any, and heals its HP by the same amount as the applied damage.\nWith this ability declared, a character trapped inside can escape only by de-bonding (see ML, p. 71) (if no declaration of [ 🗨 Hold On] has been made, the character can escape automatically at the beginning of its turn).\nIf de-bonding causes the character to escape from the inside, the effect of the Defense increase is also lost."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Magic Iron Ingot (680G / Gold Black A)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 10","loot":"Binding Chain (500G / Black A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Jet-black Binding Chain (3000G / Black S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Iron Maiden","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"O9HjRwYA910xxSd4","name":"Skeleton","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:skeleton","level":1,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Cemetery","reputation":6,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead) +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"8","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR I p. 416","description":"A walking bone corpse filled with mana. Their entire body is made of bones and usually armed with weapons, shields, and armor. They appear in old battlefields, poorly buried cemeteries, and catacombs, and will attack anyone who approaches them. They may follow more powerful undead and attack the living in packs.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"2 (9)","damage":"2d","evasion":"2 (9)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":15,"max":15},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Bone Body","description":"A Skeleton is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 10","loot":"Sturdy Bones (30G/Red B)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Magical Bones (250G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Skeleton","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Pipl8JGhUjsaWT1I","name":"Lanternhead","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lanternhead","level":6,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Barbaric, Arcana","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"-/12(Floating)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR III p. 364","description":"This former Humanoid's head is the only undead part of its body, drifting in midair. The entire head is enveloped in a blue luminescence, attacking all living things without regard. At times, it can use the Divine Magic of Immortal Queen Zeides .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":48,"max":48},"mp":{"value":42,"max":42}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 6 Level/Magic Power 8 (15)","description":""},{"title":"⏩ Fear Curse/8 (15)/Willpower/Half","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Target ,&quot; Lanternhead whispers a word of fear curse into the &quot;Target: 1 Character's&quot; ear and inflicts 1d magical damage to the target MP.\nUsing this ability consumes 3 points of MP. Also, once the target succeeds in Willpower, it cannot be used on this turn."},{"title":"◯ Nimble","description":"Lanternhead gains a +2 bonus to the Evasion check against ranged attacks."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Missing Bones (80G/Red B)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Tainted Skull (300G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lanternhead","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"PrPqqHE4JxTPaVnc","name":"Restirigist","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:restirigist","level":3,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common","habitat":"Various","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"-/10 (Floating)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"BM","description":"This undead is the result of hatred and refusal to die. At the moment of its demise, the inability to accept its own death resonates with the surrounding mana, transforming it into a pseudo-monster.\n\nUnlike ordinary Ghosts , it has no clear purpose and is filled only with resentment toward the cause of, and denial of, its own death. Since it loses its power when it leaves the place where it died, it does not travel but continues to spread its hatred and spill its &quot;truth&quot; on the spot, which is said to transform the mana around it and create a hatred-filled space.\n\nAs with the Ghost, the power of the Restirigist depends on the power of the person in the previous life (the values here are for regular Restirigist), but its intellect is reduced, so it cannot cast spells.\n\nThey might vanish if you make them aware of their death, but you can always just destroy them instead.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Smash","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+2","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":25,"max":25},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"⏩ Binding Chains of Hatred / 10 (17) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Target,&quot; curses &quot;Target: 1 Area (5m radius / All)&quot;. The targets receive a -1 penalty to all Action Checks. The area (Simplified Combat) and center coordinate (Standard and Advanced Combat) of this effect can only be targeted from the exact location where the monster itself died.\nThis ability has the Curse type and can only be used once per round.\nTranslator's Note: 10 (17) is probably a mistake in the original. My guess would be it should be 3 (10)."},{"title":"◯ Binding Grudge","description":"If the monster moves more than one area (Simplified Combat) or 5m (Standard and Advanced Combat) from the point where this Undead previously died, it will receive a -2 penalty to all action checks.\nLoot |\nNothing |\n<div"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Restirigist","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"QcljvAqamJWwu9Xc","name":"Plague Zombie","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:plague-zombie","level":2,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":8,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (Deals damage instead) +3","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"BM","description":"This is a Zombie carrying a plague in its body. Its claws can make their victim catch their plague. The disease turns its victims into new Zombies. In some cases, entire villages have been turned into Zombies because of a lack of proper response.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"3 (10)","damage":"2d+1","evasion":"2 (9)","defense":1,"hp":{"value":14,"max":14},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Plague Claws / 4 (11) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If the target is hit by a Claws attack, the target falls victim to a disease called the Wight Plague. If the target fails the Fortitude Check, one of the target's ability score, (randomly selected) is reduced by one point at the moment of the attack and every full day thereafter. This effect is cumulative. When any ability score becomes 0, the target dies and becomes a new Plague Zombie.\nThis effect is of the Disease type and lasts until the victim is healed by some means or becomes a Plague Zombie. Even if the target dies from an effect other than this disease, the progression of the disease does not stop, and in some cases, the target may become a Plague Zombie long after death."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 3","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"4 - 5","loot":"Zombie Eye (30G / Red B)"},{"roll":"6+","loot":"Zombie Eye (30G / Red B) x2"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Plague Zombie","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"R3JLjfxz4J4wr7g0","name":"Skeleton Fighter","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:skeleton-fighter","level":4,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magical","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":6,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead) +3","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"18/-","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"DA","description":"Skeletons are undead creatures that arise when mana inhabits bones after death. Skeleton Fighters are armed with weapons, shields, and armor and possess higher combat abilities than regular skeletons.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":28,"max":28},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Bone Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Sturdy Bones (30G / Red B)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magical Bones (250G / Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Skeleton Fighter","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"RbE39nvd4sOaDVIE","name":"Suicide Abyss Sword","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:suicide-abyss-sword","level":5,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness, Labyrinths","reputation":12,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 129","description":"Similar to the Suicide Sword , this is a warrior who fell in battlefields and labyrinths and became Undead. Their origin can be traced to a knight of the Holy Iron Chain Kingdom who wielded a weapon imbued with Abyss Enhancement (see CR II p. 245, AB p. 38).\n\nConsumed by the power of the Abyss, they see everything they encounter as an enemy and forcefully draw out their weapon's power to fight.\n\nThe stats define this monster's weapon's Abyss Enhancement and Abyss Curse as &quot;Accuracy +1&quot; and &quot;Vulnerable,&quot; but the GM can modify these as they see fit. Additionally, the &quot;Veteran's Weapon&quot; obtained as loot can be set up as a specific Abyss Enhancement weapon.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Abyss Sword","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":40,"max":40},"mp":{"value":18,"max":18}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Abyss Curse: Vulnerable","description":"When this monster receives magical damage, it automatically takes +1 additional point of damage."},{"title":"►Raging Abyss Blade / 7 (14) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Whirling the weapon like a storm with &quot;Range: Caster&quot; deals 2d+1 points of Curse magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 Area (3m radius) / 5.&quot;"},{"title":"⏩Submit to the Abyss","description":"Recklessly draws power from the Abyss through the weapon.\n[►Raging Abyss Blade] changes from &quot;Range: Caster&quot; to &quot;Range: Touch&quot; (cannot exclude self from targets), resistance changes from &quot;Evasion/Negates&quot; to &quot;Willpower/Half&quot;, and damage dealt changes to 2d+4 points.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"If this monster's HP is reduced to 0 or below by magic damage, the loot Veteran's Weapon cannot be obtained."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Veteran's Weapon (1,000G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Suicide Abyss Sword","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"SAyyPhlFdj7sunKA","name":"Giant Zombie","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:giant-zombie","level":15,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":13,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"25","fortitude":"20 (27)","willpower":"18 (25)","source":"CR III p. 371","description":"Giant Zombie is born from the corpse of a Giant . These are just a few examples of Giant Zombies, and the strength of Giant Zombies varies greatly depending on the race and the individual.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon (Upper Body)","accuracy":"19 (26)","damage":"2d+20","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":16,"hp":{"value":132,"max":132},"mp":{"value":20,"max":20}},{"style":"Kick (Lower Body)","accuracy":"20 (27)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"16 (23)","defense":18,"hp":{"value":142,"max":142},"mp":{"value":10,"max":10}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 10 points","description":"At the end of each round, each section of Giant Zombie recovers 10 HP. This has no effect if the section has 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Upper Body","description":""},{"title":"► War Cry/18 (25)/Willpower/Negates","description":"The Giant Zombie unleashes a powerful yell, causing fear for &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: 2-3 areas (10m Radius) / All&quot;. This fear, treated as a Psychic effect, gives a -2 penalty to all Action rolls for the next 30 seconds (3 rounds).\nThis effect is treated as Psychic type."},{"title":"🗨 Simultaneous Attack","description":"A Giant Zombie's Weapon can attack all characters in the same skirmish. Each Accuracy Check is made with a -2 penalty."},{"title":"Lower Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"A Giant Zombie's height prevents enemies from attacking it. The Upper Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. This effect disappears when the Lower Body falls to 0 HP or lower."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Giant Rotting Weapon (500G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Gold Bracelet (5,000G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Giant's Treasure (10,000G/Gold SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Giant Zombie","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"SoEUsJiGWeOYkOOo","name":"Wight","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:wight","level":4,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Silver Weapon Damage +3","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"12/-","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Battle Mastery p. 128","description":"A Wight is a vile Undead whose extremities have rotted to the bone. Its signature red eyes and bloated, discolored body are telltale signs of this foul creature.\n\nOriginally thought to be the risen bodies of those who died in water, the bony claws of a Wight don't just poison the body but curse the soul of those they rend through. Rumors tell that a powerful Wight's claws may be used as ritual tools, though what rituals are better left unsaid.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claw","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":31,"max":31},"mp":{"value":10,"max":10}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Claw / 5 (12) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If a Claw attack hits and deals at least 1 point of applied damage, it deals an additional 3 Poison magic damage to both the target's HP and MP."},{"title":"◯ Wight Curse","description":"Anyone reduced to 0 HP or below by the Wight's attack is automatically cursed without any Resistance Check.\nThe victim can recover from its unconscious state only after the curse is lifted. If left unattended, one Soulscar will be accumulated for every three days (72 hours) that pass. If the fifth Soulscar is acquired by this fact, the character immediately becomes a Wight.\nA Success Value of 14 or more is required to remove this curse by magic or other means. The character does not lose any Soulscars accumulated by this effect when the curse is removed."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Wight Claw (50G / Red B)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Cursed Claw (400G / Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Wight","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Tv6V7kYct0guQULa","name":"Rotten Wanderer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rotten-wanderer","level":10,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Regional Dialect","habitat":"Ruins, Caves","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR II p. 376","description":"This is a Humanoid Undead whose whole body is rotting. It has large bumps at the joints of their bodies, and their entire bodies are bloated with them.\n\nThey appear mainly in ruins and caves. It is not difficult to locate its territory because it rots surrounding plants just by passing through them, and its remains are covered with decaying flesh spilled from its body.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Head Butt (Head)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":99,"max":99},"mp":{"value":15,"max":15}},{"style":"Arm (Right Arm)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":74,"max":74},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}},{"style":"Arm (Left Arm)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":74,"max":74},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}},{"style":"Kick (Legs)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":91,"max":91},"mp":{"value":14,"max":14}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity , ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Spitting Rot/12 (19)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Spits out a large amount of rotten fluid from its mouth at &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5&quot; with &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Shot &quot;, dealing 2d+10 Disease magic damage."},{"title":"Right Arm/Left Arm","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Cleave II","description":"It attacks with a weapon up to 5 characters within the skirmish in which it resides."},{"title":"Legs","description":""},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = Impossible • +4","description":"This monster's sheer size hinders attack.\nThe Head cannot be attacked in melee. Against any ranged attacks, Head receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks.\nWhen the Legs fall to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Decaying Flesh (20G/Red B) x 2d"},{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Rotten Fluid (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Fizzing Rotten Fluid (1,200G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rotten Wanderer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"UhpV5A8FKjlCifE9","name":"Dark Hierophant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dark-hierophant","level":18,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana, Drakish, Basilisk, Daemonic","habitat":"Ruins, Abyss","reputation":25,"weakness":28,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":25,"movementSpeed":"18 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"22 (29)","willpower":"23 (30)","source":"CR III p. 372","description":"This is an evil hierophant, who worshipped and glorified the evil gods, and became undead by involving their followers. Even in death, they are still worshipped by the souls of the dead.\n\nThe hierophant themself has no special abilities, though they are a high priest. However, they are strengthened by the palanquin that carries them, and their power baptizes the living into death and makes them new believers.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Cane (Body)","accuracy":"22 (29)","damage":"2d+24","evasion":"21 (28)","defense":14,"hp":{"value":161,"max":161},"mp":{"value":206,"max":206}},{"style":"Fist (Palanquin)","accuracy":"24 (31)","damage":"2d+21","evasion":"20 (27)","defense":16,"hp":{"value":145,"max":145},"mp":{"value":26,"max":26}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"► Divine Magic 15 Level/Magic Power 23 (30)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Double Cast ], [ Critical Cast II ], and [ Rune Master ]."},{"title":"Palanquin","description":""},{"title":"► 3 Attacks (Free)","description":"A countless number of ghosts swarm and attack three times per round, with separate Accuracy checks and choosing whether to attack the same target again or a different target."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • +4","description":"The Body cannot be attacked in melee. Against any ranged attacks, Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks.\nThis effect disappears when the Palanquin section falls to 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Wall of Believers","description":"The Body section cannot be a target for the effects with &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, &quot;Target: 1 Character X&quot;, and &quot;Target: X area (YY radius)/Z&quot; unless it wishes to be (it still can be targeted by &quot;Target: 1 Entire Character&quot; and &quot;Target: X area (YY radius)/All).\nThis effect is lost when the Palanquin section HP falls to 0 or less."},{"title":"► Praise the Hierophant","description":"The departed sacrifice themselves and offer distorted prayers to the being above the palanquin. This ability costs 10 HP and MP to the Palanquin section.\nThe Body section heals HP and MP by 10 points immediately and gets a +2 bonus to action checks for 10 seconds (1 round)."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Holy Symbol of the Evil God (600G/Black White A) x 2d"},{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Hierophant's Cloak (11,100G/White SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dark Hierophant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"UwZ6MD8ObNc5ivDQ","name":"Dryout Corpse","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dryout-corpse","level":8,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common","habitat":"Desert","reputation":15,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 126","description":"This is a dried-up figure wandering through deserts of the Burlight Region. This Undead is believed to be the remains of those who have died in distress. They are desperately thirsty and when they spot a living creature, they pounce on it and attempt to claw and drain it for water.\n\nThe uncommon loot drop &quot;Rehydrated Monster Remains&quot; are utilized to create the &quot;Monster Bait&quot; (see Natural History of Burlight p. 43).","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":63,"max":63},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Water/Ice Absorption","description":"A Dryout Corpse is immune to Water/Ice-Type damage and effects, and instead healed for the applied Water/Ice-Type damage dealt. In this case, the monster is automatically put into [◯Rehydration State]."},{"title":"►Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two Claws attacks each round, though each attack requires its accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯Water Sucking Claws","description":"If the character is hit by a Claw attack, the Dryout Corpse's HP is recovered by the same amount as the applied damage. At the same time, this monster enters the [◯Rehydration State].\nIf the target of the Claw attack has no body fluids (such as a Fluorite or Golem, up to GMs), this effect does not occur."},{"title":"◯Rehydration State","description":"If this monster enters this state, the following effects are applied:\nAccuracy check is increased by +1, and damage is increased by +4.\nEvasion is reduced by -1.\nFire type damage is increased by +3 points.\nThis status will end when at least 1 applied damage of the Fire type is received."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"The Loot &quot;Rehydrated Monster Remains&quot; is only obtained from Dryout Corpses who are killed in a [◯Rehydration State]."},{"title":"◯Psychic Immunity, ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Rehydrated Monster Remains (900G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Tainted Bones (50G/Red B)"},{"roll":"7+","loot":"Tainted Skull (300G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dryout Corpse","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"W0DKMvZy5efIwxwI","name":"Zombie Dog","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:zombie-dog","level":1,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Labyrinths, Ruins","reputation":6,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead) +3","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"BM","description":"These wolves and dogs have been animated with mana. They have lost their natural agility and are smaller than Humanoids, so they are not a serious opponent even for novice adventurers.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"3 (10)","damage":"2d+1","evasion":"2 (9)","defense":1,"hp":{"value":14,"max":14},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 3","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"4 - 7","loot":"Zombie Eye (30G / Red B)"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Zombie Eye (30G / Red B) x2"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Zombie Dog","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"WBUUWjOmPGUfRxC8","name":"Abyss Regret","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:abyss-regret","level":2,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery Damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"-/10(Flying)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"AB, p. 97","description":"It is said that in the Shallow Abysses, the lingering regrets of those who died merged together to become these Undead.\n\nMultiple orb-like spheres about 30cm in size, resembling fire, fly while leaving trails behind them, circling in a circumference of about 1m in diameter.\n\nOminous patterns appear inside this circle, and occasionally, it is said that the regretful wishes that created this monster manifest themselves as visions.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"&#32;","defense":4,"hp":{"value":0,"max":0},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight","description":"An Abyss Regret receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"►Cry of Wishes / 3 (10) / Willpower / Negates","description":"To use this effect, consume 6 MP points. At &quot;Range/Area: 1(10m) / Target &quot;, showers &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; with cursed words. If the target fails their Willpower, they receive 2d points of Curse magic damage."},{"title":"►Moan of Wishes / 3 (10) / Willpower / Negates","description":"At &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Target &quot;, make &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; hear words of curse.\nIf the target fails their Willpower check, they receive 1 point of Curse fixed damage."},{"title":"◯Death Throes Wish / 3 (10) / Willpower / Negates","description":"This effect automatically triggers once per turn at the start of the turn when this monster's current HP is 6 points or less.\nAt &quot;Range: Caster&quot;, throws cursed words of wishes at &quot;Target: 1 area (3m radius) / 5.&quot; Characters other than those classified as &quot;Undead&quot; who fail their Willpower receive a -1 penalty to all skill checks for 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is Curse + Psychic type and does not stack."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Crystal Tears of Regret (250G/White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Abyss Regret","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"YFWuda2nFsYhqGok","name":"Flying Hands","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:flying-hands","level":4,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness, Ruins","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"-/20(Flying)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR III p. 363","description":"This is simply an undead pair of hands flying around from the elbow to the tip. It is said that the hands move only in search of the enemy as if they are wandering around in regret for the death of a fighter who could not exert their strength in battle.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist (Right Arm)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":29,"max":29},"mp":{"value":9,"max":9}},{"style":"Fist (Left Arm)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":29,"max":29},"mp":{"value":9,"max":9}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Decoy Attack I","description":"It gains -2 to Accuracy checks, but the damage is increased by +2 on hit.\nIf the declared attack is evaded, the enemy receives a -1 penalty to Evasion checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is cumulative up to - 4 but is lost if the target fails an Evasion check even once."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 11","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Yellowed Golden Ring (1,000G/Gold White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Flying Hands","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"YhBrX1Lorlmr9dr1","name":"Ghost Horse","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghost-horse","level":10,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":15,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage + 3 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"36 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 142","description":"A pitch-black horse made of shadow with a mane of flames, the Ghost Horse is dangerous on its own but is often seen as a mount for more powerful undead. Its eyes are a piercing blood-red, and its body will occasionally have gouts of flame burst forth.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Hoof (Front)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":87,"max":87},"mp":{"value":23,"max":23}},{"style":"Hoof (Rear)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":77,"max":77},"mp":{"value":18,"max":18}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Shadow Body","description":"When in shadowy areas or at night, the Ghost Horse automatically melds with the shadows, becoming impossible to see without Darkvision. While unnoticed, it can also move through otherwise solid obstacles, such as walls and barriers.\nHowever, while being seen by a character, this unique skill is lost."},{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity , ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Front","description":""},{"title":"► Burning Gaze/13 (20)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"The Ghost Horse gazes with &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Target &quot; and &quot;Target: 1 Character,&quot; igniting the target and dealing 2d + 10 Fire magic damage."},{"title":"Rear","description":""},{"title":"► Kick Away/13 (20)/Evasion/Negates","description":"The Ghost Horse unleashes a double-barrel kick on a character in the same skirmish area. The character is kicked to the rearguard area (Simplified Combat) or to any direction chosen by the monster (Standard/Advanced Combat) at 20m, and falls down with &quot;20&quot; points of fall damage."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Fiery Hoof (500G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Evil Eye (400G/Red A)"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Fiery Evil Eye (800G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Incandescent Evil Eye (3,000G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghost Horse","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Z5B0h7IZoAhKdSCi","name":"Dragon Zombie","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dragon-zombie","level":20,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":20,"weakness":27,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +4 points","initiative":21,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"27 (34)","willpower":"27 (34)","source":"CR III p. 372","description":"Dragon Zombies are the reanimated corpse of a dragon that decayed over a number of years and returned to unlife after being corrupted. Typically, Dragon Zombies are of lower intelligence due to their brain having decomposed over the years, but rarely are there intelligent Dragon Zombies capable of speech and magic. However, the organs that would produce fire in a living dragon have rotted and decayed, and now the Dragon Zombie can only exhale a rotten miasma.\n\nOften, Dragon Zombies have some sort of unfinished business in the world of the living, whether to get revenge on their slayer, to protect the remnants of their plundered horde, or something else altogether. The need to take care of this business drives the Dragon Zombie to the point where nothing will stand in their way in order to accomplish their goals.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"25 (32)","damage":"2d+24","evasion":"25 (32)","defense":18,"hp":{"value":187,"max":187},"mp":{"value":61,"max":61}},{"style":"Claw (Body)","accuracy":"26 (33)","damage":"2d+22","evasion":"22 (29)","defense":20,"hp":{"value":218,"max":218},"mp":{"value":54,"max":54}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"23 (30)","damage":"2d+20","evasion":"23 (30)","defense":15,"hp":{"value":156,"max":156},"mp":{"value":51,"max":51}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"23 (30)","damage":"2d+20","evasion":"23 (30)","defense":15,"hp":{"value":156,"max":156},"mp":{"value":51,"max":51}},{"style":"Tail (Tail)","accuracy":"24 (31)","damage":"2d+22","evasion":"23 (30)","defense":19,"hp":{"value":184,"max":184},"mp":{"value":49,"max":49}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Miasma Vortex","description":"The Dragon Zombie is surrounded by a protective veil of miasma and gains a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against ranged attacks."},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 10 points","description":"At the end of each round, each section of Dragon Zombie recovers 10 HP. This has no effect if the section has 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Poison Breath/25 (32)/Fortitude/Half","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot &quot; and &quot;Target: 1 area (6m Radius) / 20&quot;, it breathes putrid gas dealing 2d+25 Poison magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"A Dragon Zombie can make two Claw attacks each round. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯ Miasma Claws/24 (31)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"The target is weakened if the target is hit by a Claw attack. Target's strength is reduced by -6.\nThis effect is permanent and accumulative; a character whose strength falls to 0 or less dies without making a Death Check.\nIn the case of a fixed value character, each time it is affected by this effect, its damage is reduced by -1, and it will die if it is affected by the effect (Monster Level/5 (rounded up) + 2) times in total.\nThis effect is of the Disease type."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"A Dragon Zombie's height prevents enemies from attacking it. The Head receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. When the Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"🗨 All-Out Attack","description":"A Wing can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty."},{"title":"Tail","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. An Accuracy check is made on all characters at once, and damage is determined individually.\nThis attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Decaying Dragon Scales (10,000G/Red SS)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Dragon Jewel (7,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Dragon Jewel (7,000G/Red S) x 2"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Dragon's Treasure (20,000G/Gold SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dragon Zombie","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ZXSZfJZosW3B6hjv","name":"Mad Blood","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:mad-blood","level":10,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Regional Dialect","habitat":"Various","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"17","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 143","description":"This is a more powerful Blood Sucker . It is rumored that only the most powerful Nosferatu can create these monsters.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":93,"max":93},"mp":{"value":16,"max":16}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Double Attack","description":""},{"title":"⏩ Gaze/11 (18)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Mad Blood may attempt to paralyze with &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (50m)/ Target &quot;. If the target fails to resist the Gaze, they are paralyzed for 10 seconds (1 round) and cannot take any Minor Actions or declare Active Combat Feats.\nThis unique skill can be used only once per round."},{"title":"► Vampire Bite/12 (19)/Evasion/Negates","description":"The Mad Blood bites the target, dealing 2d+9 Physical damage. The Mad Blood heals HP equal to the applied damage dealt."},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 6 points","description":"At the end of each round, a Mad Blood recovers 6 HP. This has no effect if the Mad Blood is at 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Vampire Body","description":"As long as a Mad Blood is under sunlight, it takes 6 magic damage at the end of its turn and receives a -2 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion Checks. This damage cannot be reduced in any way. Additionally, the Mad Blood cannot use their [ ◯ Regeneration] unique skill."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Corrupted Ash (300G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Old Cloak (200G/White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Mad Blood","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"a6iuEGLMCCfb5HCW","name":"Cursed Artist","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cursed-artist","level":12,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"15 (22)","source":"CR III p. 368","description":"This is a figure of a past musician who could not let go of their obsession with their own music and became undead, continuing to perform even after their death. This is the result of a musician of the Magic Civilization Period who tried to use their strong spellsongs.\n\nThey are eccentric and stubborn and will not tolerate anyone who interferes with their playing. They are known to have several types of musical instruments in their hands, including a large keyboard. There are various theories about the source of their obsession, the musician or the instrument.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bow for Playing (Musician)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":115,"max":115},"mp":{"value":88,"max":88}},{"style":"None (Instrument)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"15 (22)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":106,"max":106},"mp":{"value":48,"max":48}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Concealed Main Section","description":"The Main Section of this monster is randomly selected from Musician and Instrument section at the time of its appearance and is kept secret.\nIn the Monster Knowledge check during Combat Preparation, if the success value is equal to or greater than the Weakness, in addition to applying weak points, Main Section will be identified."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], and [ Hawk Eye ]."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Musician","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 11 Level /Magic Power 14 (21)","description":""},{"title":"◯ Intoxicated by Music","description":"The body is activated in response to spellsongs .\nIf the Musician section is under the effect of any spellsong, its HP is recovered by 8 points at the end of its turn."},{"title":"Instrument","description":""},{"title":"► Basic Spellsongs 10 Level/15 (22)/All Areas (50m Radius)","description":"In addition to Basic 5th level Spellsongs , it can use [ Dare ]."},{"title":"► [Finale: Dance of the Fire Dragon]/15 (22)/Willpower/Half","description":"It uses [ Finale: Dance of the Fire Dragon ] at &quot;Range: 2 (50m)&quot;, dealing 2d+15 Fire and Wind magic damage to up to 5 targets.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Magic Repeat","description":"The same magic cast by the Musician section in the same round is cast by the Instrument section with the exact same target and the same success value. The same amount of MP is consumed from the Instrument section."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Baffling Sheet Music (800G/White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10 - 12","loot":"Vintage Instrument (2,600G/Green White S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Antique Instrument (12,600G/Green White SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cursed Artist","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"bE27h5pvQWWGmRWK","name":"Specter","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:specter","level":8,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Labyrinths, Cemetery","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"-/18 (Flying)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 373","description":"A Specter is believed to be the spirit of a powerful and angry magic user. Often, these spellcasters lived during the age of the Magical Civilization, the Magic Civilization period, and their sheer hatred of the living has kept their form intact. In fact, this hatred drives the Specter to kill anyone it comes across. For some reason, Specters will only be found at night and disappear during the day. However, unlike some others, the sun does not damage the Specter.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":66,"max":66},"mp":{"value":60,"max":60}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 8 Level/Magic Power 12 (19)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10 - 12","loot":"Old Cloak (200G/White A)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Ancient Robe (3,300G/White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Specter","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"dSpxDKPlWhgVPyJA","name":"Wraith","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:wraith","level":13,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Arcana","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":16,"weakness":23,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":25,"movementSpeed":"-/26 (Floating)","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"19 (26)","source":"CR III p. 369","description":"A Wraith is a body from which the soul has departed and become animated. It can manifest as a living agglomeration or as a dead rift after the physical body's death, rendering it unresponsive. Wraiths cannot pass through walls but can traverse small spaces. They are immune to physical attacks but can be harmed by silver and magic weapons.\n\nEach Wraith's strength varies depending on the individual before becoming a Wraith. When a Conjurer uses the [ Wraith Form ] spell, they take on this form. Some individuals become Wraiths by receiving the same effect as magic from magic-powered items or traps. These Wraiths cannot return to their bodies and remain as Wraiths.\n\nWhether the caster is dead or alive makes no difference. However, a dead Wraith can be dispelled by magic or by removing the effect to return to the body, while a live one cannot. The Wraith's body core is cold to the touch, and in rare cases, its magic power can freeze and form a gem.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":118,"max":118},"mp":{"value":112,"max":112}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Knowledge = Conjurer Class","description":"Those with Conjurer will automatically succeed in the Monster Knowledge check for this monster. But they still must roll to know its weak point."},{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 13 Level/Magic Power 18 (25)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"A Wraith can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Fog Body","description":"Blunt weapons treat the Wraith's Defense as 5 points higher.\nIn addition, the Throw weapon deals no damage to it.\nThe Wraith automatically halves the total damage of any incoming Magical damage (or quarters if the spell has &quot;Resistance: Half&quot;)."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 12","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Frozen Mana (5,000G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Wraith","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"fihA1xYifTVyq1or","name":"Ghoul","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghoul","level":3,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":8,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"11","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 134","description":"A Ghoul is an undead that eats rotting corpses. Their &quot;prey&quot; is left to decay for a while after the kill, so that the Ghoul can feed off of the rot and corruption. Compared to Zombies, a Ghoul decays at a much slower rate due to the toxin in their system. When the toxin is extracted from the body, it can be used on wood to preserve it.\n\nAdditionally, the amber sediment inside a Ghoul's eye can be extracted and solidified into a small disc, which has taken the colloquial name &quot;ghoul coin&quot; among collectors of such objects.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+2","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":30,"max":30},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Double Attack","description":"It can attack the same target twice in one action with its Claws."},{"title":"◯ Paralyzing Poison/5 (12)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If a Claw attack hits and deals at least 1 applied damage, the target has a -2 penalty to Evasion checks for 30 seconds (3 rounds). This effect is not cumulative.\nThis effect is Poison type."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Ghoul Toxin Extract (20G/Gold Red B)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Ghoul Coin (300G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghoul","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"fyCiWFxmZnGbJlDa","name":"Ghost","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghost","level":2,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common","habitat":"Various","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"-/10 (Floating)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR I p. 417","description":"Ghosts are a manifestation of the thoughts of the dead and dying, given an ethereal form after their original body has passed away. They retain their appearance in life and what knowledge they have learned over their lifetime, though this may be of questionable usefulness as time passes.\n\nIt also has memories, but most of them are distorted. The strength varies greatly from class to class and from one individual to another (the values given here are those of an ordinary person turned into a Ghost without any particular class, etc.). So, GM might change Ghost data to account for a specific individual.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Smash","accuracy":"3 (10)","damage":"2d","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":20,"max":20},"mp":{"value":20,"max":20}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Tempting Lure/4 (11)/Willpower/Negates","description":"The Ghost whispers to &quot;Target: 1 Entire Character&quot; in &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m)/ Target &quot;. If the target fails to resist, the Ghost may have that character move according to the Ghost's whim.\nAffected characters cannot move very quickly and cannot use magic or attack. If the Ghost does not order the character to move, the character will stand in position unconscious.\nThis effect is treated as a psychic type (weak) and lasts for 1 day."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 11","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Crystal Tears of Resentment (500G/White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghost","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"gLUdgAmON1CVFVsT","name":"Iceman","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:iceman","level":6,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Regional Dialect","habitat":"Cold Regions","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR II p. 371","description":"This is a monster who died in a snowfield or a snowy mountain and became undead. Except for the pale discoloration and coldness of the skin, it looks almost the same as before its death. The blocks of ice cling to various parts of their former equipment, and they sometimes attack with ice blocks by throwing them, freezing anything they touch.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":49,"max":49},"mp":{"value":25,"max":25}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Snow and Ice Mastery","description":"On snow and ice, it has no penalties due to poor footing."},{"title":"► Throw Ice Block/9 (16)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Throws a block of ice at &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; with &quot;Range: 1 (100m)&quot;, dealing 2d+8 water/ice physical damage."},{"title":"◯ Freeze/Can't","description":"If a fist attack or [ ► Throw Ice Block] hits, it will freeze the opponent. This is treated as a Petrifaction (Dexterity or Agility/-6) effect.\nThis effect is Water/Ice type. Also, if the target receiving this effect has HP or MP being reduced by a Fire type effect, this effect will be removed entirely.\nIf its Dexterity or Agility reaches 0, the target becomes completely petrified (frozen)."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 11","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Ice Crystal (1,600G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Iceman","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"gyKrZ2SLIqMNITgZ","name":"Phantom Horse","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:phantom-horse","level":6,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands, Wilderness","reputation":12,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (when deals damage) +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"25 (Flying)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 130","description":"This is the Phantom of a horse that died on the battlefield near Eyutorgo in the Ursyla Region.\n\nIt sometimes wanders the former battlefield, perhaps searching for its fallen jockey or cursing the enemy who separated them.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Kick","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":40,"max":40},"mp":{"value":18,"max":18}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Gain a +1 bonus modifier to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks."},{"title":"►Undead Blessing / 6 (13) / Optional","description":"With &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: 2-3 Areas (10m radius) / All,&quot; empowers Undead characters other than itself. Targets receive a +2 bonus modifier to Accuracy checks and +2 points to damage for 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is of Curse type and does not stack."},{"title":"►Neigh for a Jockey / 8 (15) / Willpower / Negates","description":"With &quot;Range: Caster&quot; at &quot;Target: All Areas (20m radius)/All,&quot; releases a cry seeking a jockey.\nHumanoid or Barbarous characters who fail their Willpower check take 2d+3 points of magic damage. Furthermore, on their next turn, they must approach this monster by any means possible. They will move toward the same position (area, coordinate) and attempt to minimize the distance between them even if they cannot reach it. If Normal Move is insufficient, they will use Full Move, and if they can move using items or magic, they will use those as well (the final ruling is up to the GM). There are no restrictions on actions after movement.\nThis effect is of the Curse + Psychic type. This forced movement effect persists for 10 seconds (1 round). It has no effect whatsoever, including damage, on characters other than &quot;Category: Humanoid&quot; and &quot;Category: Barbarous&quot;. Additionally, it cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"If a character under the duration of [►Neigh for a Jockey] deals weapon attack damage to this monster, they will not obtain the loot Bond-Deep Reins."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Bond-Deep Reins (600G/White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"Old Horse Clothing (200G/White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Aged Horse Clothing (800G/White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Phantom Horse","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"hrBA8VeR7brUEjcc","name":"Suicide Sword","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:suicide-sword","level":5,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness, Underground Labyrinths","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2","initiative":7,"movementSpeed":"15/-","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"BM","description":"These Undead wield powerful magic swords imbued with holy power. Most of the weapons these creatures bear have been found to be swords, but some also wield axes, spears, and fist weapons. When defeated, their holy swords shatter and are lost, but leave behind Sword Shards as loot.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Sacred Sword","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":40,"max":40},"mp":{"value":18,"max":18}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Sacred Blade Rampage / 6 (13) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Flourishes its blade like a raging tempest, at &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; &quot;Target: 1 Area (3m radius/5),&quot; dealing 2d+1 Energy magic damage."},{"title":"⏩ Draw Forth Power","description":"Calls forth power from the sacred blade without regard for itself.\nFor 10 seconds (1 round), the Resistance Check for [ ► Sacred Blade Rampage] changes from Evasion/Negates to Fortitude/Half, and the damage becomes 2d+4.\nWhen it uses this effect, the Sword immediately receives 5 points of fixed damage to its HP and its Evasion is penalized by -1 for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Sword Shard x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Sacred Sword Hilt (1,000G / White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Suicide Sword","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ig3XgTev485HRDY4","name":"Ancient Ghost","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ancient-ghost","level":15,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Regional Dialect, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":16,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2","initiative":22,"movementSpeed":"-/16 (Floating)","fortitude":"19 (26)","willpower":"18 (25)","source":"BM","description":"This monster is a powerful Undead that was created with magic from the grudges of the dead from before the Magic Civilization Period. It is extremely rare to encounter them as they are few and buried inside deep dungeons and ruins.\n\nLike the Ghost , some of them have past knowledge and memories, but their memories are from so long ago that even the source of their hatred is often unclear. Their goals are fuzzy and may appear and disappear from time to time. It is said that if their true desire is identified and fulfilled, their memories will return, and they will disappear.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"17 (24)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":184,"max":184},"mp":{"value":184,"max":184}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"The Ancient Ghost can perform 2 Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"► Tempting Lure/17 (24)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Whispers temptation to &quot;Target: 1 Entire Character&quot; in &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m)/Target&quot;. If the target fails the Willpower check, the Ancient Ghost may have that character move according to its own whim. If no instructions are given, the target will just stand there. A target under this effect moves slowly and cannot make any attack or cast a spell.\nThis effect is treated as Psychic type (Weak) and lasts for one day."},{"title":"⏩ Fear Aura/18 (25)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Whispers sinisterly to &quot;Target: All Areas (50m Radius)/All&quot; within &quot;Range: Caster&quot;, causing them to cower in fear. Targets that fail the Willpower check take a -2 penalty to its Success Value when making melee, shooting attacks or casting a spell against this monster or while in a skirmish containing this monster against any other character inside. If a character fails the Willpower check with a Success Value of 21 or less, they must move as far as possible to get out of range of this unique skill (If the movement is blocked by a skirmish area they need to prepare to withdraw). This effect is treated as Psychic type, and lasts for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis unique skill can be used only once per round.\nLoot |\nNothing |\n<div"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ancient Ghost","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"khTf0naUcXBqqxCj","name":"Poisonous Wight","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:poisonous-wight","level":11,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":15,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Silver Weapon Damage +3","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"17","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"BM","description":"A type of Wight , a corpse in a state of total decomposition. In addition to the paralytic power of its rotten claws, the poisonous gas stored within its body damages anything in its vicinity. Poisonous Wights are mindless and attack living creatures to try to increase the number of its allies. Because it has no feelings or logic, its behavior is unpredictable.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claw","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":99,"max":99},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Robe of Poisonous Fog/Can't","description":"A Poisonous Wight constantly releases a green poison fog from its mouth and nose and covers &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / Space&quot; within &quot;Range: Caster&quot;. Anyone in the area suffers 2d Poison magic damage at the start of their turns."},{"title":"◯ Paralyzing Poison/14 (21)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If a Claw attack hits and deals at least 1 applied damage, the target has a - 2 penalty to Evasion checks for 30 seconds (3 rounds). This effect is not cumulative.\nThis effect is of a Poison type."},{"title":"◯ Poison Claw/14 (21)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Poisonous Wight hits with a claw attack and inflicts one or more points of applied damage, the target suffers an additional 7 points of Poison type damage to its HP and MP."},{"title":"◯ Wight's Curse/Can't","description":"Anyone reduced to 0 HP or below by the Wight's attack is automatically cursed, without any Resistance Check.\nOnly after the curse is lifted can the victim recover from its unconscious state. If left unattended, one Soulscar will be accumulated for every three days (72 hours) that pass. If the fifth Soulscar is acquired by this fact, the character immediately becomes a Wight .\nA Success Value of 20 or more is required to remove this curse by magic or other means. The character does not lose any Soulscars accumulated by this effect when the curse is removed."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 4","loot":"Wight Claw (50G / Red B)"},{"roll":"5 - 7","loot":"Cursed Claw (400G / Red A)"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Poisonous Claws (1600G / Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Poisonous Wight","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"kxJySQJRW2V3fpgD","name":"Burning Iceman","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:burning-iceman","level":7,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade common","habitat":"Graves, Shallows","reputation":13,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15/-","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"AB, p. 98","description":"It is an Undead with an abnormal appearance, where its right half is scorched and wrapped in flickering fire, joined with its frozen left half.\n\nWhen obtaining loot from this monster, you will get a Fire Crystal from the Right Half section and an Ice Crystal from the Left Half section.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fire Fist (Right Half)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"&#32;","defense":9,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Ice Fist (Left Half)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"&#32;","defense":9,"hp":{"value":8,"max":8},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"►Ice-Fire Piercing Breath / 9 (16) / Fortitude / Half","description":"This effect can only be used when both Right Half and Left Half sections are alive and before taking a Major Action. When used, both sections take 5 points of fixed damage each and end the turn.\nReleases a spiraling stream of cold and fire with &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) /[ [| Line]]&quot;, dealing 2d+10 points of Water/Ice and Fire types magic damage to the target.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"Right Half","description":""},{"title":"◯Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Water/Ice Vulnerability","description":"When the Right Half is hit by Water/Ice-type damage, it takes an extra 3 damage."},{"title":"◯Fire Fist","description":"Fire Fist attacks are treated as Fire type physical damage."},{"title":"Left Half","description":""},{"title":"◯Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Fire Vulnerability","description":"When the Left Half is hit by Fire-type damage, it takes an extra 3 damage."},{"title":"◯Ice Fist","description":"Ice Fist attacks are treated as Water/Ice type physical damage."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Fire/Ice Crystal (1,600G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Burning Iceman","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"lsBc0vRQ2NcJUzZ9","name":"Ghoul Mage","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghoul-mage","level":5,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Regional Dialect, Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":10,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 136","description":"Seemingly identical to the Ghoul , a Ghoul Mage has the intellect to understand human speech. They prefer to live at the same level as humans, and despite being Ghouls, they eat fresh meat and often use it to trap creatures.\n\nRarely will one find a Ghoul Mage with enough mana that it even crystallizes in the &quot;Ghoul Coin.&quot; These high-quality coins glitter with an unearthly pattern and will undoubtedly fetch quite the price to the right collector.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":38,"max":38},"mp":{"value":24,"max":24}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 4 Level / Magic Power 7 (14)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."},{"title":"► Double Attack","description":"It can attack the same target twice in one action with its Claws."},{"title":"◯ Paralyzing Poison/5 (12)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If a Claw attack hits and deals at least 1 applied damage, the target has a -2 penalty to Evasion checks for 30 seconds (3 rounds). This effect is not cumulative.\nThis effect is Poison type."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Ghoul Toxin Extract (20G/Gold Red B)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 11","loot":"Ghoul Coin (300G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Rare Ghoul Coin (350G/Gold A) x 1d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghoul Mage","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"mGd8juCvVV9yWMGi","name":"Bone Hound","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bone-hound","level":4,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead) +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"VC","description":"A Bone Hound is an Undead grotesque quadruped. Its body is stripped of flesh, except for the face, the only remaining part. The skeletal creature is unnervingly agile and emits poison from its face, which still clings to putrid flesh.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":27,"max":27},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}},{"style":"Tail (Body)","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":33,"max":33},"mp":{"value":14,"max":14}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Poison Breath/6 (13)/Fortitude/Half","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m)/Shot,&quot; spits poison at &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, dealing 2d+2 poison magic damage.\nThis effect cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 3 targets in the same skirmish. This ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Beast Skull (60G/Red B)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Twisted Bones (130G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bone Hound","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"odBIMmu0MbLFhsYN","name":"Abyss Dead Hound","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:abyss-dead-hound","level":8,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness, Graveyards, Shallows","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"19 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"AB, p. 99","description":"An Undead creature wrapped in blue-purple fire that also breathes it from its mouth, taking the form of a massive hunting hound. Its fur is mangy, and half of its skin has melted away.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"&#32;","defense":10,"hp":{"value":7,"max":7},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"►Flame Breath / 10 (17) / Fortitude / Half","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Shot &quot;, breathe fire on &quot;Target: 1 area (Radius 4m) / 10&quot;, dealing 2d+12 points of Fire magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯Fire Bite","description":"Bite attacks are treated as Fire-type physical damage."},{"title":"◯Corrosive Flame / Can't","description":"If this monster deals 12 or more points of applied damage during its turn, the target(s) that received the damage (all targets if multiple) receive a -1 penalty to Fortitude, Willpower and Death checks.\nThis effect is Curse type and stacks if received multiple times, lasting until this monster is defeated.\nIf forced removal of this effect is desired, the Success Value is 15."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Corrupted Ash (300G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Tainted Bones (50G/Red B)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Tainted Skull (300G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Abyss Dead Hound","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"oxGQdgN1InbJy9Ua","name":"Shadow of the Shard","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:shadow-of-the-shard","level":4,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Energy Damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"-/12 (Floating)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"AB, p. 97","description":"If one carelessly touches an Abyss Core or Abyss Shard, they may be devoured by darkness that erupts from within. These are the souls of the deceased who were afflicted by the curse of the Shallow Abyss, having become &quot;black shadows&quot; that possess others.\n\nThese are Undead that hate all living things. They sharpen their shadows into weapon-like forms to strike.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"7(14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"&#32;","defense":6,"hp":{"value":3,"max":3},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Abyss Gap / 12 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"Shadow of the Shard lurks in the shadows of Abyss Cores and Abyss Shards. When approaching within 10m of these (or this monster), failing a Danger Sense check with Target Number 12 results in being ambushed."},{"title":"◯Abyss Curse / 6 (13) / Willpower / Negates","description":"This effect automatically triggers once during combat initiation, immediately after &quot;Combat Preparation&quot; and right before the Monster Knowledge check.\nWith &quot;Range: Caster&quot; it applies an Abyss Curse to &quot;Target: All Areas (30m radius) / All.&quot; However, characters that fall under any of these categories are immune: &quot;Habitat includes 'Shallows',&quot; &quot;Classification: Daemon ,&quot; or &quot;Race is Abyssborn .&quot;\nThose who fail their Willpower check must immediately roll once on the Abyss Curse table (see AB p. 42) and apply the results. This persists regardless of &quot;equipped/carried&quot; conditions until this monster is defeated.\nIf multiple instances of this monster appear and Abyss Curses are received from multiple sources, Willpower checks are made in order for each instance. Only one Abyss Curse is received from the last failed check.\nThe Abyss Curse disappears when that specific Shadow of the Shard is defeated. Any earlier Willpower check failures are ignored. This effect is Curse type."},{"title":"►Black Needle of the Abyss / 6 (13) / Willpower / Half","description":"To use this effect, consume 6 MP points. With a &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m)&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, launches a needle that appears as a black shadow, dealing 2d+4 points of Curse magical damage."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Crystallized Tears of Regret (250G/White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Shadow of the Shard","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pgW8KltOWWpxcEAY","name":"Corpse Mass","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:corpse-mass","level":8,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Regional Dialect","habitat":"Ruins, Battlefields","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR III p. 365","description":"The souls of warriors who died without redemption have merged and become Undead. The corpses of the warriors can move and wield weapons, but their bodies are anchored in the mysterious light they carry, which connects each warrior seamlessly.\n\nThey have lost most of their sense of self, but they can still communicate. They harbor a deep hatred of the living and are willing to fight as slaves if they are promised to kill the living. However, if they feel that promises are not kept, and their desire to kill is not fulfilled, they immediately begin to rebel.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None (Colored Light)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":71,"max":71},"mp":{"value":52,"max":52}},{"style":"Weapon (Corpse x 3+)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":63,"max":63},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Cursed Light","description":"A character who makes a melee attack against this monster, regardless of success or failure, suffers 3 curse fixed damage for each attempt."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Colored Light","description":""},{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ HP Sharing","description":"Whenever this section receives damage to HP, half of the applied damage (rounded up) is allocated as fixed damage to any Corpse section so that the section itself receives only the rest of the damage. The damage cannot be allocated to a Corpse section whose HP is already 0 or less, but it is acceptable if the HP of the Corpse section becomes 0 or less as a result of the allocation."},{"title":"► Raise Dead","description":"Resurrects one Corpse section whose HP is 0 or less, with the maximum HP.\nUsing this ability consumes 20 points of MP of the Colored Light section."},{"title":"Corpse","description":""},{"title":"◯ Coordinated Attack","description":"If an attack on a Corpse section is evaded, the other Corpse section's attacks on that target gain a +1 to the Accuracy check against that target. This modifier is accumulated for each evaded attack. However, once any Corpse section attack hits or the monster's turn is ended, it is lost."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Crystal Tears of Resentment (500G/White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Dirty Weapons (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"7+","loot":"Engraved Weapon (600G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Corpse Mass","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"prKtd4PPRJvur5jr","name":"Dullahan Lord","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dullahan-lord","level":11,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana, Magitech","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":17,"weakness":24,"weakPoint":"Energy damage +3 points","initiative":22,"movementSpeed":"40 (Wheeled)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"CR III p. 367","description":"An improved Dullahan , the Dullahan Lord still wears beat-up white armor and tucks its head underneath one arm.\n\nHowever, the Dullahan Lord is familiar with Magitech and takes advantage of an ancient Manabike instead of the old horse-drawn carriage.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Sword (Rider)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":95,"max":95},"mp":{"value":123,"max":123}},{"style":"Slam (Manabike)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":101,"max":101},"mp":{"value":43,"max":43}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Iron Body","description":"The Dullahan Lord is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity , ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Rider","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Divine Magic , Magitech 11 Level/Magic Power 15 (22)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"A Dullahan Lord can use the Combat Feats [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Rune Master ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike II","description":"They can deal an additional +12 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"Manabike","description":""},{"title":"► Magitech 11 Level/Magic Power 15 (22)","description":""},{"title":"► Gunfire/14 (21)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Has a gun with &quot;Range: 2 (30m)&quot; and Maximum Capacity of 5."},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Stray shots cannot occur."},{"title":"► Sonic Blaster/15 (22)/Fortitude/ Neg","description":"Within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; causes a loud noise around the target, impacting &quot;Target: All Areas (30m Radius) / All&quot;. Targets suffer 2d bludgeoning magic damage and cannot declare Minor Actions or active combat feats for 10 seconds (1 round). Their Accuracy check and Evasion check are penalties by -2.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Downswing","description":"The Rider section deals an extra +2 damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used when the Manabike falls to 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • None","description":"The Manabike's size hinders attack.\nThe Rider cannot be attacked with Melee Attacks. When the Manabike falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Manabike Parts (500G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Mithril (2,600G/Gold S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Pure Mithril (8,800G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dullahan Lord","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pvvRDJhQuxT2T489","name":"Dullahan","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dullahan","level":7,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":11,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead) +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"25 (4 Legs &amp; Wheeled)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR I p. 419","description":"A Dullahan is an immense figure comprised of a headless knight in black armor, driving a hellish chariot pulled by skeletal horses.\n\nIt carries its head in its left arm and sentences a man to death in one year. Anyone who tries to prevent a Dullahan from doing so becomes a target themselves (though they may not be killed until a year later). It is unclear why Dullahans do what they do, but even if their target hides in a secret room or on an isolated island, the Dullahan always appears and attempts to kill them.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Sword (Rider)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":53,"max":53},"mp":{"value":44,"max":44}},{"style":"Charge (Chariot)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":62,"max":62},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Hoof (Horse)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":37,"max":37},"mp":{"value":22,"max":22}},{"style":"Hoof (Horse)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":37,"max":37},"mp":{"value":22,"max":22}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"Rider","description":""},{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Divine Magic 5 Level / Magic Power 8 (15)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], and [ Violentcast I ]."},{"title":"Chariot","description":""},{"title":"◯ Iron Body","description":"The Chariot is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • None","description":"The Chariot's size hinders attack.\nThe Rider cannot be attacked in melee. When the Chariot falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."},{"title":"Horse","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Less Mobile","description":"Each time the HP of a Horse section falls to 0 or below, the Dullahan movement is reduced by -10."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 4","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"5 - 7","loot":"Magical Wood (200G/Gold Green A)"},{"roll":"8 - 12","loot":"Premium Magical Wood (500G/Gold Green A)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Mithril (2,600G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dullahan","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pyFl6qN2dsZDwJtg","name":"Gratuna's Whale Fall","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gratunas-whale-fall","level":9,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Lakesides, Oceans","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15 (Crawling) / 15 (Swimming)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 127","description":"These are Undead versions of large marine creatures such as enormous fish, whales, and sea turtles. Their entire bodies are decayed, with skeletons so deteriorated that it's difficult to maintain their body shape, but they can operate in shallow waters, coastlines, and lakeshores for short periods.\n\nMost of them have remained motionless on the sea or lake bottom for hundreds of years or more. Their bodies have become habitats for smaller fish, which may suddenly burst out from inside them.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":72,"max":72},"mp":{"value":34,"max":34}},{"style":"Front Legs (Front)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":84,"max":84},"mp":{"value":21,"max":21}},{"style":"Rear Legs (Rear)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":72,"max":72},"mp":{"value":21,"max":21}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."},{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":"There are no restrictions or penalties for actions in water."},{"title":"◯Attitude Control","description":"It does not fall prone under any effect."},{"title":"◯Weak to Recovery Effects","description":"When HP is reduced by a healing effect, an additional 3 points will be reduced."},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = +4•+4","description":"Size hinders attacks. The Head section gains a +4 bonus to Evasion against Melee Attacks and Ranged Attacks.\nThis effect is lost if the HP of either the Front or Rear section drops to 0 or below."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If the effect of [◯Overflowing] has been activated three times, the &quot;Fermented Fish School&quot; loot will be lost."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"►Filth Spew / 11 (18) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Spews out rotten flesh and other filth from the mouth. Deals 2d+8 points of magic damage to targets within &quot;3m radius (1 area)/5&quot; centered on self. Targets who fail their resistance also suffer a -1 penalty to Evasion, Fortitude, and Willpower for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect is treated as Disease type for both damage and penalty. This effect cannot be used in consecutive turns and cannot be used in the same turn as the unique skill [►Collapse] from the Front section."},{"title":"◯Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +8 points."},{"title":"Front","description":""},{"title":"►Collapse / 11 (18) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Collapses its entire body, crushing surrounding enemies.\nTargets within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;1 Area (6m radius) / All&quot; receive 2d+14 points of physical damage. When using this effect, the Front section receives a -2 penalty for Evasion for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect cannot be used in consecutive turns and cannot be used in the same turn as the Head section unique skill [►Filth Spew]."},{"title":"◯Overflow / Can't","description":"Small creatures that had been living in the stomach overflow and scatter, fleeing in all directions. At the start of the Front section's turn, roll 1d. If the result is 3 or higher, creatures overflow from the stomach and scurry around the feet. Targets within &quot;Radius 6m (1 area) / All&quot; centered on oneself receive 1d fixed damage and suffer a -1 penalty to Evasion.\nThis effect is treated as Disease type for both damage and penalty modifiers. This effect can only be triggered up to 3 times (if the roll is 1 or 2, the effect is not triggered)."},{"title":"Rear","description":""},{"title":"◯Double Attack","description":"The Rear Legs attack the same target twice."},{"title":"◯Regeneration","description":"If the HP of the Head or Front sections is 1 or more, at the end of its turn, the HP of those sections will recover by 5. This effect will be lost if the HP of the Rear section falls to 0 or less."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Fermented Fish School (600G/White A) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Rotten Fluid (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Fizzing Rotten Fluid (1,200G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gratuna's Whale Fall","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"qBk0vFJu6E34C2QS","name":"Rotten Beast","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rotten-beast","level":11,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Tombs","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"25 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 144","description":"These are mythical beasts whose entire bodies have decayed and become undead. The majority are quadrupeds, but some of them fly in the sky or move underwater.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":133,"max":133},"mp":{"value":20,"max":20}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Double Bite","description":"When dealing damage with a Bite attack, the damage is rolled twice and added during damage calculation."},{"title":"► Miasma Breath/13 (20)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Rotten Beast spits miasma with &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Shot &quot; to &quot;Target: 1 area (4m Radius) / 10&quot;, dealing 2d+14 Disease magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Skull of a Defiled Mythical Beast (1,500G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rotten Beast","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"qjnEIWQsyU99A7Ic","name":"Grudge Wight","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:grudge-wight","level":6,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":13,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Silver Weapon Damage +3","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"13/-","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"BM","description":"A Wight born with a stronger grudge than a normal Wight. Although it appears indistinguishable from a Wight, it possesses enlarged claws that have the ability to bestow curses on the target they strike.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claw","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":50,"max":50},"mp":{"value":15,"max":15}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Claw / 8 (15) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If a Claw attack hits and deals at least 1 point of applied damage, it deals an additional 5 poison magic damage to both the target's HP and MP."},{"title":"◯ Grudge Wight's Curse","description":"Anyone reduced to 0 HP or below by the Grudge Wight's attack is automatically cursed, without any Resistance Check.\nOnly after the curse is lifted can the victim recover from its unconscious state. If left unattended, one Soulscar will be accumulated for every three days (72 hours) that pass. If the fifth Soulscar is acquired by this fact, the character immediately becomes a Grudge Wight.\nA Success Value of 16 or more is required to remove this curse by magic or other means. The character does not lose any Soulscars accumulated by this effect when the curse is removed."},{"title":"► Grudge Return / 7 (14) / Willpower / Half","description":"At &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; with &quot;Range/Area: 2 (30m)/Target,&quot; the Wight expresses its resentment for taking damage. The target will be dealt (20 - the monster's current HP) (minimum 1) Curse magic damage (just 20, not Power 20)."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Wight Claw (50G / Red B)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Cursed Claw (400G / Red A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Sinister Cursed Claw (1,070G / Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Grudge Wight","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"sKFeqQNzLpKdVYPy","name":"Frost Zombie","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:frost-zombie","level":3,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Cold, Ruins","reputation":8,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (when deals damage) +3 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 129","description":"These are monsters that were once Humanoid and Barbarous corpses who perished in cold regions, now reanimated as Undead. Their bodies remain frozen in a state of decay, with most retaining their physical form intact, and they move more nimbly than typical Undead.\n\nTheir claws have grown enlarged and hardened with ice and mana, and one may sustain serious wounds without realizing they've been injured.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":2,"hp":{"value":28,"max":28},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Freezing Claws / 5 (12) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"When a Claw attack hits, the target must make a Fortitude check. On failure, they take &quot;1d-1 (minimum 1)&quot; points of magical damage and suffer a -1 penalty to Accuracy checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is Water/Ice type."},{"title":"◯ Melting Body","description":"If the creature takes even 1 point of applied Fire-type damage, the [ ◯ Freezing Claws] ability is lost, and Defense is reduced by 2 points."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"If the [ ◯ Melting Body] effect triggers during combat, the creature will not drop the &quot;Ice Claw&quot; loot."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Zombie Eye (30G/Red B) x 2"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Ice Claw (200G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Frost Zombie","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"sMRVWkBRF2bTRQ8A","name":"High Revenant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:high-revenant","level":0,"monsterType":"","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Inherited from previous life","habitat":"Various","reputation":12,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":-2,"movementSpeed":"※","fortitude":"※ +2","willpower":"※ +2","source":"CR II p. 373","description":"They are creatures resurrected by powerful hatred or obsessions from the dead.\n\nThe significant difference from the regular Revenant is that it retains almost all of its original knowledge and memories. It is often distorted by delusions, but you can converse with High Revenants and negotiate with them. However, they are rarely interested in anything other than relief from their own grudges.\n\nHigh Revenants can be created from Humanoids, Barbarous, Animals, or Mythical Beasts of Adventurer Level or Monster Level 7 or higher.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon, etc.","accuracy":"※ +2","damage":"※ +2","evasion":"※ -2","defense":0,"hp":{"value":0,"max":0},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 8 points","description":"At the end of each round, the High Revenant recovers 8 HP. This has no effect if High Revenant has 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Past Life","description":"This monster's strength depends on its strength before it is reborn as a High Revenant.\nIn the various numerical fields, apply the numerical value of the monster before it was reborn to the places marked with &quot; ※ &quot; The level of this monster is equal to &quot;Previous Level + 1&quot;.\nHigh Revenant also inherits combat feats and unique skills and spells."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Tainted Skull (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Tainted Bones (50G/Red B)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Tainted Sacrum (2,400G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"High Revenant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"sSBcMJzvHHFUPFZB","name":"Poltergeist","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:poltergeist","level":8,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":11,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"-/16 (Floating)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"BM","description":"Poltergeists are entities that form when an individual dies while holding an unnaturally strong attachment to a particular object. This object becomes the core of the Poltergeist, regardless of its nature, and allows the spirit to manipulate other objects to affect the living world.\n\nCommon Poltergeist cores (Main Section) include various pieces of jewelry, favored items of the original owner, or other innocuous mementos, such as toys and dolls. The commonality of these objects facilitates the Poltergeist's ability to hide its core among other objects it manipulates. However, only the core of the Poltergeist can cast spells or manipulate other objects, so it becomes apparent where the core is when combat begins.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam (Core)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":75,"max":75},"mp":{"value":51,"max":51}},{"style":"Slam (Object)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":60,"max":60},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}},{"style":"Slam (Object)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":60,"max":60},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}},{"style":"Slam (Object)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":60,"max":60},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}},{"style":"Slam (Object)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":60,"max":60},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Object Camouflage","description":"A Poltergeist's Core is indistinguishable from the other Object sections it is using at the start of combat. At the beginning of the combat, the GM keeps secret which of the 5 sections is a Core section and which is an Object section.\nHowever, once the Core uses any spells, or either the [ ► Command Weapon] or [ ► Rush] unique skills are used, the Core can be easily identified.\nMelee attacks don't directly identify the Core, but knowledgeable characters are able to make conclusions based on the damage received."},{"title":"Core","description":""},{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 8 Level/Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"A Poltergeist can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Metamagic/Area ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"► Command Weapon/Can't","description":"At &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/Target&quot; and &quot;Target: 1&quot;, the Poltergeist possesses a weapon. The target is attacked with the weapon it has equipped and automatically suffers damage. The damage is &quot;Weapon's Power + 8&quot; points. Characteristics such as Power, Critical Threshold, type, etc., depend on the individual weapon. It is applied if the weapon has a constant effect, but special effects activated by a password, MP consumption, etc., do not occur.\nThis unique skill cannot command any Gun category weapon. If the controlled weapon is of the Bow or Crossbow category, the ammunition used will be one randomly chosen from those that the person holding the weapon has available in their quiver."},{"title":"Object","description":""},{"title":"► Rush/Can't","description":"Within &quot;Range: Touch,&quot; all remaining Object sections simultaneously rush at a &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, &quot;dealing 2d x (Remaining Objects)&quot; physical damage to the target.\nAll remaining Objects must be able to take a Major Action to use this unique skill, and using this ability counts as a Main Action for all Objects once completed."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Broken Mementos (500G / White A)"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Mementos (1,000G / White S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Enchanted Object (2,000G / Gold White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Poltergeist","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"t6cq9gF4fNXYTfaX","name":"Skeleton Guardian","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:skeleton-guardian","level":7,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR II p. 372","description":"This is a heavily-armed Skeleton . When it is hit, it shatters, and its bones fly off, blocking the opponent's view, drawing attention, and aiding the attacker.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":61,"max":61},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Bone Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Bone Dance","description":"If Skeleton Guardian has 40 or less HP remaining, it gains a +2 bonus to Accuracy checks. If it has 25 or less HP remaining, the bonus increases to +4. If it has 15 or less HP remaining, its weapon always hits."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 4","loot":"Sturdy Bones (30G/Red B)"},{"roll":"5+","loot":"Magical Bones (250G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Skeleton Guardian","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"uPPBaUKog34Ma4mm","name":"Death Sword","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:death-sword","level":4,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness, Labyrinths","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR II p. 370","description":"A tortured spirit trapped within a sword, the Death Sword possesses a decaying body to carry out its foul grudges. When encountering a stronger opponent, the Death Sword will seek to slay the stronger and possess that body, so it often looks for stronger and stronger foes to face.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":36,"max":36},"mp":{"value":18,"max":18}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Blade of Death/5 (12)/Evasion/Negates","description":"The Death Sword slashes a &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; within &quot;Range: Touch&quot; with a vengeful blade, dealing 10 Curse magic damage."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Rusty Sword (50G/Black White B)"},{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Ornate Sword Hilt (600G/White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Death Sword","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"wQuopoFdPvDm5HuB","name":"Mummy Lord","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:mummy-lord","level":11,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"CR II p. 377","description":"It is believed that, in ancient times, royal families from the Magic Civilization period would often have themselves bound and buried in ornate crypts to keep their family together and protect them from what may lie beyond. A Mummy Lord is unliving proof of such claims and wields incredible power to preserve the family's crypt. Able to command other Mummies that were buried alongside them, a Mummy Lord also has great combat prowess and magical power at its command.\n\nWhile a Mummy Lord is typically only roused from its slumber to deter any intruders into the crypt, there are stories of large armies of the undead attacking settlements under the watchful eye of a Mummy Lord.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Cane","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":92,"max":92},"mp":{"value":75,"max":75}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 10 Level/Magic Power 14 (21)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Decaying Curse","description":"If a Cane attack hits, it will reduce the target's maximum HP by the same amount as the applied damage (never less than 0). If a character's maximum HP is reduced to 0 in this way, they immediately die (no Death Check needed).\nThis effect is treated as a curse type and is permanent. This effect can also be removed with a spell such as the [Remove Curse] spell (which requires a success value of at least 22), but it is automatically removed if the Mummy Lord who bestowed the curse is defeated. A character who dies with a maximum HP of 0 can only be revived after removing the curse."},{"title":"◯ Fire Vulnerability","description":"When the Mummy is hit by Fire-type damage, it takes an extra 3 damage."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Staff of the Wizard-King (3,000G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Yellowed Golden Ring (1,000G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"8 - 12","loot":"Yellowed Golden Bracelet (2,000G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Golden Mask (15,000G/Gold White SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Mummy Lord","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"wisD0IJHZyFbmKsi","name":"Skeleton Archer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:skeleton-archer","level":4,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":6,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR II p. 369","description":"It is a Skeleton armed with a bow and arrows. It responds to any approaching creature with relentless fire.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":28,"max":28},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Bone Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"► Bow","description":"With &quot;Range: 2 (30m),&quot; it makes a Shooting Attack with a bow, Accuracy check, and damage are the same as a normal attack."},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Stray shots cannot occur."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Sturdy Bones (30G/Red B)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magical Bones (250/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Skeleton Archer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xc3ODe4EynlTGjsH","name":"Phantom","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:phantom","level":5,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common","habitat":"Various","reputation":10,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead) +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"-/11 (Floating)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR I p. 418","description":"A Phantom is the consciousness of someone that has died, leaving behind a strong grudge. It reacted with mana and became Undead. It takes on the form of a living being, but has no substance and wanders about covered in a white cloth.\n\nThey hate the living with a passion and attack them to welcome new members into the ranks of the undead. This resentment is feared because it curses and debilitates the living and empowers the undead, giving them more power and increasing their threat.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fists","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":42,"max":42},"mp":{"value":16,"max":16}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Undead Blessing/5 (12)/Optional","description":"It empowers other undead characters within &quot;Range: Self&quot; and &quot;Target: 2-3 area (10m radius / All)&quot;. The targets receive a +2 bonus for Accuracy checks and +2 points to damage for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect is a curse type."},{"title":"► Hateful Scream/7 (14)/Willpower/Half","description":"Phantom emits a cursed cry to the living at &quot;Range: Self&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 area (6m radius) / All&quot;. All targets except for the undead are dealt 2d+2 Curse magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Old Cloak (200G/White A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Ancient Cloak (800G/White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Phantom","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xuTXFFPiHzBA2itT","name":"Ghoul Lynx","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghoul-lynx","level":4,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountains","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14 (4 legs)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 124","description":"This is a Grey Lynx which has become a corpse-eating Undead. It is a dangerous monster that devours its prey by weakening it with Paralyzing Poison.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":2,"hp":{"value":28,"max":28},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Continuous Attack II","description":"If a Ghoul Lynx successfully hits a target in melee, they may make a second attack. They can make a third attack against the same target if a second attack hits."},{"title":"◯Paralyzing Poison / 6 (13) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If a Bite attack hits and deals at least 1 applied damage, the target has a -2 penalty to Evasion checks for 30 seconds (3 rounds). This effect is not cumulative. This effect is Poison type."},{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity, ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Ghoul Toxin Extract (20G/Gold Red B)"},{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Antiseptic Fur (600G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghoul Lynx","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"yDB42fKhUSmJKC0h","name":"Blood Swamp","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:blood-swamp","level":9,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Swamps, Forests","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"10 (Fluid)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 141","description":"This is an irregularly shaped mass of reddish-black liquid. It is believed to be the result of the thoughts of people who have sunk into bottomless swamps. The liquid moves about and constantly changes its shape. It can harm living beings due to its toxic composition.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":72,"max":72},"mp":{"value":40,"max":40}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Attitude Control","description":"It does not fall prone under any effect."},{"title":"◯ Morphogenesis","description":"It is constantly wriggling and changing its form.\nAt the beginning of its turn, roll 1d, and for 10 seconds (1 round), the damage is increased by the rolled value, and Defense is decreased by the rolled value."},{"title":"⏩ Blood Strike/10 (18)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Within &quot;Range: Touch&quot;, Blood Swamp showers &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; with his/her own blood, dealing 2d magic damage and blinding it for 3 minutes (18 rounds). This effect is Poison type. This effect can be used only once per 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Gem (150G/Gold A) x 1d"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Memento (800G/Gold Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Blood Swamp","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"yhBFpQYl468sCdGM","name":"Abyss Skeleton Guard","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:abyss-skeleton-guard","level":9,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Shallow","reputation":15,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery Damage (when deals damage), +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"21","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"AB, p. 99","description":"This is an Undead creature that is the reanimated skeletal corpse of a large Barbarous skilled in handling weapons.\n\nIt is said to have been created by the Shallow Abyss itself to protect the Abyss Core, but there are many cases where they are controlled by Barbarous, who dwell near the Core.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Sword (Right Arm)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"&#32;","defense":12,"hp":{"value":9,"max":9},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Hammer (Left Arm)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"&#32;","defense":12,"hp":{"value":9,"max":9},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Kick (Lower Body)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"&#32;","defense":11,"hp":{"value":10,"max":10},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Abyss Curse / 11 (18) / Willpower / Negates","description":"This effect automatically triggers once during combat initiation, immediately after &quot;Combat Preparation&quot; and right before the Monster Knowledge check.\nWith &quot;Range: Caster&quot; it applies an Abyss Curse to &quot;Target: All Areas (30m radius) / All.&quot; However, characters that fall under any of these categories are immune: &quot;Habitat includes 'Shallows'&quot;, &quot;Classification: Daemon &quot;, or &quot;Race is Abyssborn .&quot;\nThose who fail their Willpower check must immediately roll once on the Abyss Curse table (see AB p. 42) and apply the results. This persists regardless of &quot;equipped/carried&quot; conditions until this monster is defeated.\nIf multiple instances of this monster appear and Abyss Curses are received from multiple sources, Willpower checks are made in order for each instance. Only one Abyss Curse is received from the last failed check.\nThe Abyss Curse disappears when that specific Abyss Skeleton Guard is defeated. Any earlier Willpower check failures are ignored.\nThis effect is Curse type."},{"title":"Right Arm","description":""},{"title":"🗨Lethal Strike II","description":"The 2d roll of damage decision is increased by +1. At risk, he takes a -1 penalty to its Evasion check."},{"title":"◯Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +9 points."},{"title":"Left Arm","description":""},{"title":"🗨Aimed Attack II","description":"Gains a +2 bonus to Accuracy checks."},{"title":"Lower Body","description":""},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Size hinders attacks.\nRight Arm and Left Arm sections gain a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nThis effect is lost when the Lower Body section's HP falls to 0 or below."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Large Weapon (300G/Black White A) x 2"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Magical Bones (250G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"6 - 8","loot":"Magical Bones (250G/Gold Red A) x 1d"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magical Bones (250G/Gold Red A) x 2d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Abyss Skeleton Guard","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"yo7SoAjvSeeubqX6","name":"Jack O'Lantern","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:jack-olantern","level":7,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":13,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"HP Recovery (deals damage instead), +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"-/18(Flying)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 139","description":"This is a pumpkin-headed monster dressed in a black veil. They wear white gloves and hold a scythe in both hands, which is larger than their height, and attack with the scythe.\n\nThey haunt and roam the remote villages at night, looking for victims. When they kill their prey, they are said to light up their mouths and eyes with bright lights.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Scythe","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":58,"max":58},"mp":{"value":36,"max":36}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Summoning Arts 6 Level/Magic Power 9 (16)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Metamagic/Distance ], [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Soul Harvesting","description":"If the target is reduced to 0 HP or lower from a Jack O'Lantern's Scythe attack, they receive a -10 penalty to their next Death Check."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type (Weak) Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Unstable Healing","description":"Healing effects such as Divine Magic and items like Unicorn's Horn will damage Undead instead.\nMagitech, Fairy Magic, Nature Magic, etc. healing has no effect on the Undead.\nSpiritualism Magic and a few other healing effects can restore an Undead's HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Pumpkin Lantern (100G/Green White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Rusty Scythe (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Large Scythe (600G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Soul Harvesting Scythe (3,000G/Gold Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Jack O'Lantern","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"zyf0Fx2Yigv4clBO","name":"Implicit Grudge Wight","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:implicit-grudge-wight","level":10,"monsterType":"Undead","intelligence":"Human","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Silver Weapon Damage +3","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"16/-","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"BM","description":"Some Grudge Wights , upon their resurrection, receive the blessing of Zeides the Immortal Queen or other deities closely associated with the Undead. These more powerful individuals are termed &quot;Implicit Grudge Wights.&quot; They gain intelligence and the ability to plan and move deliberately, and even wield a limited form of Divine Magic.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claw","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":90,"max":90},"mp":{"value":55,"max":55}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Claw / 12 (19) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If a Claw attack hits and deals at least 1 point of applied damage, it deals an additional 9 Poison magic damage to both the target's HP and MP."},{"title":"◯ Grudge Wight's Curse","description":"Anyone reduced to 0 HP or below by the Grudge Wight's attack is automatically cursed, without any Resistance Check.\nOnly after the curse is lifted can the victim recover from its unconscious state. If left unattended, one Soulscar will be accumulated for every three days (72 hours) that pass. If the fifth Soulscar is acquired by this fact, the character immediately becomes a Grudge Wight (see p. 129).\nA Success Value of 20 or more is required to remove this curse by magic or other means. The character does not lose any Soulscars accumulated by this effect when the curse is removed."},{"title":"► Grudge Return / 11 (18) / Willpower / Half","description":"At &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; with &quot;Range/Area: 2 (30m)/Target,&quot; the Wight expresses its resentment for being hurt. The target will be dealt (36 - the monster's current HP) (minimum 1) Curse magic damage (just 36, not Power 36)."},{"title":"► Limited Divine Magic/Magic Power 12 (17)","description":"Can use the Divine magic spell [ Fist of God ]. (Note the Zeides is a Major God.)"},{"title":"🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"The Grudge Wight can use the Combat Feat [ Multi-Action ]."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Strange Holy Symbol (3,300G / White S)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Cursed Claw (400G / Red A)"},{"roll":"8 - 12","loot":"Sinister Cursed Claw (1,070G / Red S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Corrupted Claw (4,800G / Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Implicit Grudge Wight","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}